[{:db/id 17592186152157 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-599b6849-3342-5594-bc18-d66421f45e91"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-599b6849-3342-5594-bc18-d66421f45e91" :question/id #uuid "599b6849-3342-5594-bc18-d66421f45e91" :question/math-academy-id "q-75983" :question/problem "The matrix $Q$ is given below. Let ${q}_{1}$, ${q}_{2}$,  ${q}_{3}$ and ${q}_{4}$ be the respective columns of $Q.$\nDetermine if $B=\\text{{}{q}_{1},{q}_{4}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(Q).$ \nIf that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${q}_{3}={x}_{1}{q}_{1}+{x}_{4}{q}_{4}.$ \n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & -30 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 24 & 14\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $Q$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & -30 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 24 & 14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=(-\\frac{1}{5}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 24 & 14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(Q)$ is $\\{{q}_{1},{q}_{2},{q}_{4}\\}.$ \n\nSo, we conclude that $B=\\{{q}_{1},{q}_{4}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(Q).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2cf517a6-abf9-5b4f-942e-0933e5866f68"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2cf517a6-abf9-5b4f-942e-0933e5866f68" :answer-field/id #uuid "2cf517a6-abf9-5b4f-942e-0933e5866f68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3bb4d8dd-5f42-53d6-b9ea-b3eb6b57a83a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0dee10fc-3dcb-5237-af24-246152c9267c" "answer-3f53ddd2-bec1-5acd-9379-2bb08043f9b8" "answer-1e13e6c1-1f37-56f8-a726-2aee62b71439" "answer-8e0920b1-977a-544d-8f3c-6269c1d5b48c" "answer-3bb4d8dd-5f42-53d6-b9ea-b3eb6b57a83a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0dee10fc-3dcb-5237-af24-246152c9267c" :answer/id #uuid "0dee10fc-3dcb-5237-af24-246152c9267c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f53ddd2-bec1-5acd-9379-2bb08043f9b8" :answer/id #uuid "3f53ddd2-bec1-5acd-9379-2bb08043f9b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e13e6c1-1f37-56f8-a726-2aee62b71439" :answer/id #uuid "1e13e6c1-1f37-56f8-a726-2aee62b71439" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e0920b1-977a-544d-8f3c-6269c1d5b48c" :answer/id #uuid "8e0920b1-977a-544d-8f3c-6269c1d5b48c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3bb4d8dd-5f42-53d6-b9ea-b3eb6b57a83a" :answer/id #uuid "3bb4d8dd-5f42-53d6-b9ea-b3eb6b57a83a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\{{q}_{1},{q}_{4}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(Q)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-594a47fa-1a44-547a-9d72-e8c6cf9a66a8" :activity/id #uuid "594a47fa-1a44-547a-9d72-e8c6cf9a66a8" :activity/title "Finding a Basis of the Column Space of a Matrix" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049009 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-80d6770d-411b-5ebd-a09b-9dd0e0ef2207" "step-41edc12e-5fa5-59e0-8507-462c39773a78" "step-3406a266-f837-5455-a9bb-cdb5eaca59e0" "step-c5d68886-09b7-5abd-b2fe-67f6c5a4497b" "step-c718742f-e154-5150-af0e-f95c2bb1c418"] :activity/first-step "step-80d6770d-411b-5ebd-a09b-9dd0e0ef2207" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-80d6770d-411b-5ebd-a09b-9dd0e0ef2207" :step/id #uuid "80d6770d-411b-5ebd-a09b-9dd0e0ef2207" :step/content 17592186435356 :step/next "step-41edc12e-5fa5-59e0-8507-462c39773a78" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-41edc12e-5fa5-59e0-8507-462c39773a78" :step/id #uuid "41edc12e-5fa5-59e0-8507-462c39773a78" :step/content "question-599b6849-3342-5594-bc18-d66421f45e91" :step/next "step-3406a266-f837-5455-a9bb-cdb5eaca59e0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3406a266-f837-5455-a9bb-cdb5eaca59e0" :step/id #uuid "3406a266-f837-5455-a9bb-cdb5eaca59e0" :step/content 17592186247222 :step/next "step-c5d68886-09b7-5abd-b2fe-67f6c5a4497b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c5d68886-09b7-5abd-b2fe-67f6c5a4497b" :step/id #uuid "c5d68886-09b7-5abd-b2fe-67f6c5a4497b" :step/content 17592186247223 :step/next "step-c718742f-e154-5150-af0e-f95c2bb1c418" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c718742f-e154-5150-af0e-f95c2bb1c418" :step/id #uuid "c718742f-e154-5150-af0e-f95c2bb1c418" :step/content 17592186500329 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186165998 :answer-field/choices 17592186166000] [:db/retract 17592186165998 :answer-field/choices 17592186166001] [:db/retract 17592186165998 :answer-field/choices 17592186166002] [:db/retract 17592186165998 :answer-field/choices 17592186166003] [:db/retract 17592186165998 :answer-field/choices 17592186165999] [:db/retract 17592186165992 :answer-field/choices 17592186165993] [:db/retract 17592186165992 :answer-field/choices 17592186165994] [:db/retract 17592186165992 :answer-field/choices 17592186165995] [:db/retract 17592186165992 :answer-field/choices 17592186165996] [:db/retract 17592186165992 :answer-field/choices 17592186165997] {:db/id 17592186166872 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-21d74430-9169-5f5c-9745-dbb6cae86953" "question-826a3dfa-4e58-52b9-b4cc-53a7b2b826d4" "question-c62464eb-da81-57d3-9709-e91e0d4b8042"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166725 :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n       \\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\cosh}{\\mathop{\\rm cosh}\\nolimits}\n \\newcommand{\\sinh}{\\mathop{\\rm sinh}\\nolimits}\n \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}$Find a hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the trigonometric identity $1 + \\cot^2{x} = \\csc^2{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n       \\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\cosh}{\\mathop{\\rm cosh}\\nolimits}\n \\newcommand{\\sinh}{\\mathop{\\rm sinh}\\nolimits}\n \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}$Osborn's rule allows us to construct a hyperbolic identity from a corresponding trigonometric identity.\n\nTo apply Osborn's rule, we follow two steps:\n\n1\\. Replace every trigonometric function with its corresponding hyperbolic function.\n\n2\\. For any product of two trigonometric sines, flip the sign of the corresponding product of hyperbolic sines.\n\nWe're given the following trigonometric identity:\n\n$$\n1 + \\cot^2{x} = \\csc^2{x}\n$$\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n\\cot^2{x} = \\dfrac{\\cos^2{x}}{\\sin^2{x}} \\qquad \\textrm{and} \\qquad \\csc^2{x} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sin^2{x}}\n$$\n\nand thus, we have two products of sines. Therefore, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is \n\n$$\n1 \\,{\\mathbf{\\color{red}{-}}}\\, \\coth^2{x} = {\\mathbf{\\color{red}{-}}}\\,\\csch^2{x}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166791 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d4fc19ee-fc09-58f6-b456-25b6d7c144cf" "question-bd25bce0-e06f-5534-8414-1587d88ad138" "question-c94b3bf4-462a-5a97-a5df-84bb2aaaa4fe" "question-b13f329b-704f-5b15-801d-b08d9d90b1ac"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166629 :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\cosh}{\\mathop{\\rm cosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sinh}{\\mathop{\\rm sinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}$\nEvaluate $\\displaystyle \\int _{-1}^{1} \\coth{x}\\sinh{x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\cosh}{\\mathop{\\rm cosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sinh}{\\mathop{\\rm sinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the trigonometric identity \n\n$$\n\\cot{x}=\\dfrac{\\cos{x}}{\\sin{x}}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is\n\n$$\n\\coth{x}=\\dfrac{\\cosh{x}}{\\sinh{x}}.\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the integral using the above identity, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{1}-{e}^{-1}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{-1}-{e}^{-(-1)}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{1}-{e}^{-1}-{e}^{-1}+{e}^{1}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2e-2{e}^{-1}}{2} \\\\  & =e-{e}^{-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166792 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5f16bf74-fd62-5389-9de5-031fc7e1da5b" "question-fb7adc98-109e-57e5-9f19-72ef71c8b698" "question-15a967e4-1f67-5afa-8031-c76c4fbb09cf" "question-ee29c156-d06d-572b-b229-09cda1e3a6dc" "question-9fa8b923-c944-5ab9-8f5d-a280f219b3bf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166630 :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\sinh}{\\mathop{\\rm sinh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\cosh}{\\mathop{\\rm cosh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\tanh}{\\mathop{\\rm tanh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int _{-1}^{1} \\dfrac{\\tanh^2{x}}{2\\sinh^2 x} \\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\sinh}{\\mathop{\\rm sinh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\cosh}{\\mathop{\\rm cosh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\tanh}{\\mathop{\\rm tanh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$First, we write our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int _{-1}^{1} \\dfrac{\\tanh^2{x}}{2\\sinh^2 x}\\textrm{d}x =\n\t\t\\dfrac{1}{2}\\int _{-1}^{1} \\dfrac{1}{\\sinh^2{x}}\\cdot \\tanh^2{x} \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow we need to find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the trigonometric identity \n\n$$\n\\tan{x}=\\dfrac{\\sin{x}}{\\cos{x}}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is  \n\n$$\n\\tanh{x} = \\dfrac{\\sinh{x}}{\\cosh{x}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the above identity to write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {tanh}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{sech}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{e-{e}^{-1}}{e+{e}^{-1}}-\\frac{{e}^{-1}-e}{{e}^{-1}+e}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{{e}^{2}+1}-\\frac{1-{e}^{2}}{1+{e}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{{e}^{2}+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{{e}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166793 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f7758d7e-a5ba-50ee-a45d-ff68b3cc6226" "question-7d070173-586a-5be7-bd5c-a4be4b18eeea" "question-b4fa5f6e-c8a3-5731-a2a2-6fc871183cc3" "question-8879f5ec-f2c2-51de-a1ef-edc8baad4b56" "question-390d417d-9926-5446-a159-d0e16ff521f1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166631 :question/problem "Evaluate \n$\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n\\displaystyle{\\int_{0}^{\\ln 3} \\tanh x   \\, \\textrm{d}x  }.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following trigonometric identity:\n\n$$\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n\\tan{x} = \\dfrac{\\sin{x}}{\\cos{x}}\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is\n\n$$\n\\tanh{x} = \\dfrac{\\sinh{x}}{\\cosh{x}}.\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u = \\cosh{x}.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\sinh{x} \\quad \\Longrightarrow \\quad \\textrm{d}u = \\sinh{x} \\, \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration according to the rule $u = \\cosh{x}.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\ln 3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\dfrac{5}{3}$ |\n\nNow, we evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{5/3}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{1}^{5/3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{3})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-21d74430-9169-5f5c-9745-dbb6cae86953" :question/id #uuid "21d74430-9169-5f5c-9745-dbb6cae86953" :question/math-academy-id "q-138950" :question/problem "$$\nFind a hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the trigonometric identity $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y).$" :question/worked-solution "$$\nOsborn's rule allows us to construct a hyperbolic identity from a corresponding trigonometric identity.\n\nTo apply Osborn's rule, we follow two steps:\n\n1\\. Replace every trigonometric function with its corresponding hyperbolic function.\n\n2\\. For any product of two trigonometric sines, flip the sign of the corresponding product of hyperbolic sines.\n\nWe're given the following trigonometric identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\n$$\n\nNotice that we have a product of sines. Therefore, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\,2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡y & =\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x-y)-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x+y) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡y & =\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x+y)-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x-y).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9e0e726d-6993-5071-a69e-aca3d0e40b18"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9e0e726d-6993-5071-a69e-aca3d0e40b18" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e0e726d-6993-5071-a69e-aca3d0e40b18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fdb9280d-9adf-5c2f-8f47-855cf75173a8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fdb9280d-9adf-5c2f-8f47-855cf75173a8" "answer-e2b713d6-928a-5284-9165-2435ed51e0dc" "answer-e9664b47-5d9b-5cc8-92fa-11c86b5da539" "answer-b73ad957-5c90-5f33-8162-155e4e01158a" "answer-4d9e97b8-e512-516e-8ae6-4de402f6b85a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdb9280d-9adf-5c2f-8f47-855cf75173a8" :answer/id #uuid "fdb9280d-9adf-5c2f-8f47-855cf75173a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡y=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x+y)-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x-y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2b713d6-928a-5284-9165-2435ed51e0dc" :answer/id #uuid "e2b713d6-928a-5284-9165-2435ed51e0dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡y=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x-y)+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x+y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9664b47-5d9b-5cc8-92fa-11c86b5da539" :answer/id #uuid "e9664b47-5d9b-5cc8-92fa-11c86b5da539" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡y=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x-y)-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x+y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b73ad957-5c90-5f33-8162-155e4e01158a" :answer/id #uuid "b73ad957-5c90-5f33-8162-155e4e01158a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡y=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(x+y)-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(x-y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d9e97b8-e512-516e-8ae6-4de402f6b85a" :answer/id #uuid "4d9e97b8-e512-516e-8ae6-4de402f6b85a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡y=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(x-y)+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(x+y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167465 :question/problem "$$\nFind a hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the trigonometric identity $\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nOsborn's rule allows us to construct a hyperbolic identity from a corresponding trigonometric identity.\n\nTo apply Osborn's rule, we follow two steps:\n\n1\\. Replace every trigonometric function with its corresponding hyperbolic function.\n\n2\\. For any product of two trigonometric sines, flip the sign of the corresponding product of hyperbolic sines.\n\nWe're given the following trigonometric identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not have a product of sines. Therefore, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186165998 :answer-field/correct "answer-81cbace4-5806-5b41-b4de-0e5c8bcb22b2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4f9358f5-ef1f-54b1-99ef-1197f59d64d0" "answer-81cbace4-5806-5b41-b4de-0e5c8bcb22b2" "answer-81e96895-4bc5-5473-8e80-cdb7431151cd" "answer-2fb53bbb-85a3-5bf3-a469-97f9b6d515c2" "answer-c9355724-e50d-561b-a5bc-0428aabebe3e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f9358f5-ef1f-54b1-99ef-1197f59d64d0" :answer/id #uuid "4f9358f5-ef1f-54b1-99ef-1197f59d64d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x=-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81cbace4-5806-5b41-b4de-0e5c8bcb22b2" :answer/id #uuid "81cbace4-5806-5b41-b4de-0e5c8bcb22b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81e96895-4bc5-5473-8e80-cdb7431151cd" :answer/id #uuid "81e96895-4bc5-5473-8e80-cdb7431151cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2fb53bbb-85a3-5bf3-a469-97f9b6d515c2" :answer/id #uuid "2fb53bbb-85a3-5bf3-a469-97f9b6d515c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x={sinh}^{2}⁡x+{cosh}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9355724-e50d-561b-a5bc-0428aabebe3e" :answer/id #uuid "c9355724-e50d-561b-a5bc-0428aabebe3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x={sinh}^{2}⁡x-{cosh}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167464 :question/problem "$$\nFind a hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the trigonometric identity ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "$$\nOsborn's rule allows us to construct a hyperbolic identity from a corresponding trigonometric identity.\n\nTo apply Osborn's rule, we follow two steps:\n\n1\\. Replace every trigonometric function with its corresponding hyperbolic function.\n\n2\\. For any product of two trigonometric sines, flip the sign of the corresponding product of hyperbolic sines.\n\nWe're given the following trigonometric identity:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nNotice that we have a product of sines. Therefore, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is \n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡x\\,-\\,{sinh}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186165992 :answer-field/correct "answer-44e24fff-6edb-58dd-b6c8-7731cb263263" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9c651855-a335-5bd9-bf70-edb22dff84f8" "answer-454d23bc-df8f-5fb0-9ac4-bbc97aefba45" "answer-4e3e4413-d9ee-532c-ae52-619bdac2ce6d" "answer-5985a81f-c958-57c9-9d4b-af828a400130" "answer-44e24fff-6edb-58dd-b6c8-7731cb263263"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c651855-a335-5bd9-bf70-edb22dff84f8" :answer/id #uuid "9c651855-a335-5bd9-bf70-edb22dff84f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{cosh}^{2}⁡x+{sinh}^{2}⁡x=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-454d23bc-df8f-5fb0-9ac4-bbc97aefba45" :answer/id #uuid "454d23bc-df8f-5fb0-9ac4-bbc97aefba45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{cosh}^{2}⁡x+{sinh}^{2}⁡x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e3e4413-d9ee-532c-ae52-619bdac2ce6d" :answer/id #uuid "4e3e4413-d9ee-532c-ae52-619bdac2ce6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{cosh}^{2}⁡x+{sinh}^{2}⁡x=e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5985a81f-c958-57c9-9d4b-af828a400130" :answer/id #uuid "5985a81f-c958-57c9-9d4b-af828a400130" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44e24fff-6edb-58dd-b6c8-7731cb263263" :answer/id #uuid "44e24fff-6edb-58dd-b6c8-7731cb263263" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-826a3dfa-4e58-52b9-b4cc-53a7b2b826d4" :question/id #uuid "826a3dfa-4e58-52b9-b4cc-53a7b2b826d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-138949" :question/problem "$$\nFind a hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the trigonometric identity $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$" :question/worked-solution "$$\nOsborn's rule allows us to construct a hyperbolic identity from a corresponding trigonometric identity.\n\nTo apply Osborn's rule, we follow two steps:\n\n1\\. Replace every trigonometric function with its corresponding hyperbolic function.\n\n2\\. For any product of two trigonometric sines, flip the sign of the corresponding product of hyperbolic sines.\n\nWe're given the following trigonometric identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\n$$\n\nNotice that we have a product of sines. Therefore, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x-y)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡y\\,-\\,\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡y.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-22b72122-c08b-57d4-b94a-a03d93b80384"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-22b72122-c08b-57d4-b94a-a03d93b80384" :answer-field/id #uuid "22b72122-c08b-57d4-b94a-a03d93b80384" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d25733c2-3d33-5bb1-aafb-e34cc2667a13" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b28508db-0cd8-544d-999a-08776558bf64" "answer-26d2fb87-73ae-5a6b-90bf-69f713e47020" "answer-08e07aea-260c-5921-8de8-d04c22d40c3a" "answer-d25733c2-3d33-5bb1-aafb-e34cc2667a13" "answer-e8748be8-b203-589d-aaf9-5ee1d5c46030"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b28508db-0cd8-544d-999a-08776558bf64" :answer/id #uuid "b28508db-0cd8-544d-999a-08776558bf64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x-y)=-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26d2fb87-73ae-5a6b-90bf-69f713e47020" :answer/id #uuid "26d2fb87-73ae-5a6b-90bf-69f713e47020" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x-y)=2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08e07aea-260c-5921-8de8-d04c22d40c3a" :answer/id #uuid "08e07aea-260c-5921-8de8-d04c22d40c3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x-y)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡y+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d25733c2-3d33-5bb1-aafb-e34cc2667a13" :answer/id #uuid "d25733c2-3d33-5bb1-aafb-e34cc2667a13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x-y)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡y-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8748be8-b203-589d-aaf9-5ee1d5c46030" :answer/id #uuid "e8748be8-b203-589d-aaf9-5ee1d5c46030" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x-y)=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡y-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c62464eb-da81-57d3-9709-e91e0d4b8042" :question/id #uuid "c62464eb-da81-57d3-9709-e91e0d4b8042" :question/math-academy-id "q-139016" :question/problem "$$\nFind a hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the trigonometric identity $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$" :question/worked-solution "$$\nOsborn's rule allows us to construct a hyperbolic identity from a corresponding trigonometric identity.\n\nTo apply Osborn's rule, we follow two steps:\n\n1\\. Replace every trigonometric function with its corresponding hyperbolic function.\n\n2\\. For any product of two trigonometric sines, flip the sign of the corresponding product of hyperbolic sines.\n\nWe're given the following trigonometric identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not have a product of sines. Therefore, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(x+y)=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡y+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡y.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-df7e218a-51b1-5a2c-9dfe-061597bffce9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-df7e218a-51b1-5a2c-9dfe-061597bffce9" :answer-field/id #uuid "df7e218a-51b1-5a2c-9dfe-061597bffce9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-36744821-b10b-57d0-9a41-509c0394e6b0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c3c639d3-b514-565a-aef9-5928de4ef0d3" "answer-36744821-b10b-57d0-9a41-509c0394e6b0" "answer-4b57663a-c099-5e3f-b686-05fdeb0b2b92" "answer-0a54b6a7-f164-57c2-9d18-a35fbbab2114" "answer-49555273-5842-5a42-a1d3-66dd471f73a6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3c639d3-b514-565a-aef9-5928de4ef0d3" :answer/id #uuid "c3c639d3-b514-565a-aef9-5928de4ef0d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(x+y)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡y-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36744821-b10b-57d0-9a41-509c0394e6b0" :answer/id #uuid "36744821-b10b-57d0-9a41-509c0394e6b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(x+y)=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡y+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b57663a-c099-5e3f-b686-05fdeb0b2b92" :answer/id #uuid "4b57663a-c099-5e3f-b686-05fdeb0b2b92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(x+y)=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡y-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a54b6a7-f164-57c2-9d18-a35fbbab2114" :answer/id #uuid "0a54b6a7-f164-57c2-9d18-a35fbbab2114" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(x+y)={cosh}^{2}⁡x+{sinh}^{2}⁡y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49555273-5842-5a42-a1d3-66dd471f73a6" :answer/id #uuid "49555273-5842-5a42-a1d3-66dd471f73a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(x+y)={sinh}^{2}⁡x+{sinh}^{2}⁡y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d4fc19ee-fc09-58f6-b456-25b6d7c144cf" :question/id #uuid "d4fc19ee-fc09-58f6-b456-25b6d7c144cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-352684" :question/problem "$$\n\nEvaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x{sech}^{3}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the trigonometric identity \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the integral using the above identity, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x{sech}^{3}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x})}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{2-{2}^{-1}}{2+{2}^{-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-\\frac{1}{2}}{2+\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{3}{2}}{\\frac{5}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f1b5624b-d189-5839-a384-dfb6d3457d12"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f1b5624b-d189-5839-a384-dfb6d3457d12" :answer-field/id #uuid "f1b5624b-d189-5839-a384-dfb6d3457d12" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-56ae9a87-b6bd-553c-894c-fb7b9c46e795" :answer-field/choices ["answer-56ae9a87-b6bd-553c-894c-fb7b9c46e795"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56ae9a87-b6bd-553c-894c-fb7b9c46e795" :answer/id #uuid "56ae9a87-b6bd-553c-894c-fb7b9c46e795" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bd25bce0-e06f-5534-8414-1587d88ad138" :question/id #uuid "bd25bce0-e06f-5534-8414-1587d88ad138" :question/math-academy-id "q-352673" :question/problem "$$\n\nEvaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identities corresponding to the trigonometric identities \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{ and }\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identities are\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\,\\text{ and }\\,\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the integral using the above identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{0}-{e}^{-0}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-{2}^{-1}}{2}-\\frac{1-1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3}{2})}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-371769d0-a8d2-5429-b519-c67818b5ff8d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-371769d0-a8d2-5429-b519-c67818b5ff8d" :answer-field/id #uuid "371769d0-a8d2-5429-b519-c67818b5ff8d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-66c4c321-c3fc-50a9-83a8-59c121c7db0d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-66c4c321-c3fc-50a9-83a8-59c121c7db0d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66c4c321-c3fc-50a9-83a8-59c121c7db0d" :answer/id #uuid "66c4c321-c3fc-50a9-83a8-59c121c7db0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c94b3bf4-462a-5a97-a5df-84bb2aaaa4fe" :question/id #uuid "c94b3bf4-462a-5a97-a5df-84bb2aaaa4fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-346474" :question/problem "$$\n\nEvaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{coth}^{2}⁡x{sinh}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identities corresponding to the trigonometric identities \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{ and }\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identities are\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\,\\text{ and }\\,\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the integral using the above identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{coth}^{2}⁡x{sinh}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {sinh}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{0}-{e}^{-0}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-{3}^{-1}}{2}-\\frac{1-1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{8}{3})}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-49a779e2-c85d-5324-8778-80dd2097d44f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-49a779e2-c85d-5324-8778-80dd2097d44f" :answer-field/id #uuid "49a779e2-c85d-5324-8778-80dd2097d44f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9a24661b-9376-5478-ba22-345b80fbea58" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9a24661b-9376-5478-ba22-345b80fbea58"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a24661b-9376-5478-ba22-345b80fbea58" :answer/id #uuid "9a24661b-9376-5478-ba22-345b80fbea58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167400 :question/problem "$$\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "$$\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the trigonometric identity \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the integral using the above identity, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{0}+{e}^{-0}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+{2}^{-1}}{2}-\\frac{1+1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186165608 :answer-field/correct 17592186165612 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-b13f329b-704f-5b15-801d-b08d9d90b1ac" :question/id #uuid "b13f329b-704f-5b15-801d-b08d9d90b1ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-352678" :question/problem "$$\n\nEvaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nFirst, we recall the following  identities:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the integral using the above identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3-{3}^{-1}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{8}{3})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c87e6d3b-23bd-5b1e-bec0-bba379741512"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c87e6d3b-23bd-5b1e-bec0-bba379741512" :answer-field/id #uuid "c87e6d3b-23bd-5b1e-bec0-bba379741512" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-25f737d4-4208-55a3-aa88-7222aded4409" :answer-field/choices ["answer-25f737d4-4208-55a3-aa88-7222aded4409"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25f737d4-4208-55a3-aa88-7222aded4409" :answer/id #uuid "25f737d4-4208-55a3-aa88-7222aded4409" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5f16bf74-fd62-5389-9de5-031fc7e1da5b" :question/id #uuid "5f16bf74-fd62-5389-9de5-031fc7e1da5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-352935" :question/problem "$$\n\nEvaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/2)}^{0}\\frac{\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/2)}^{0}\\frac{\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/2)}^{0}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow we find the hyperbolic identities corresponding to the trigonometric identities \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{ and }\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identities are\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\\,\\text{ and }\\,\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the above identities to write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/2)}^{0}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/2)}^{0}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\cdot {sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{sech}^{2}⁡x{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/2)}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{sech}^{2}⁡(0)+\\frac{1}{2}{sech}^{2}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1/2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{4}{({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡1/2}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1/2})^{2}}-\\frac{4}{({e}^{0}+{e}^{0})^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(1/2+2)^{2}}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{50}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-408af374-202e-561f-90a6-1910a956b51e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-408af374-202e-561f-90a6-1910a956b51e" :answer-field/id #uuid "408af374-202e-561f-90a6-1910a956b51e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-98919bb4-2785-53dd-9466-f9d0288a76cc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-98919bb4-2785-53dd-9466-f9d0288a76cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98919bb4-2785-53dd-9466-f9d0288a76cc" :answer/id #uuid "98919bb4-2785-53dd-9466-f9d0288a76cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{50}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fb7adc98-109e-57e5-9f19-72ef71c8b698" :question/id #uuid "fb7adc98-109e-57e5-9f19-72ef71c8b698" :question/math-academy-id "q-96265" :question/problem "${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the hyperbolic identities that correspond to the following trigonometric identities: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identities are\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csch}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x},\\,\\,\\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the above identities to express the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csch}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)+\\operatorname{csch}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}}+\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{4-{4}^{-1}}+\\frac{2}{2-{2}^{-1}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{15}+\\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2f4c241c-0bbe-5dbc-9897-1ee7bd328728"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2f4c241c-0bbe-5dbc-9897-1ee7bd328728" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f4c241c-0bbe-5dbc-9897-1ee7bd328728" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-234cc714-ee95-51d3-9f60-96338562378e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4f31d1d3-9617-5495-b1c8-0bd332072ade" "answer-529a7029-8e13-5a97-9918-a3b488d2c78c" "answer-fffb787f-ff79-5c83-b983-661bbcea077a" "answer-234cc714-ee95-51d3-9f60-96338562378e" "answer-70329641-1279-5076-9f37-fb06772be638"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f31d1d3-9617-5495-b1c8-0bd332072ade" :answer/id #uuid "4f31d1d3-9617-5495-b1c8-0bd332072ade" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-529a7029-8e13-5a97-9918-a3b488d2c78c" :answer/id #uuid "529a7029-8e13-5a97-9918-a3b488d2c78c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fffb787f-ff79-5c83-b983-661bbcea077a" :answer/id #uuid "fffb787f-ff79-5c83-b983-661bbcea077a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-234cc714-ee95-51d3-9f60-96338562378e" :answer/id #uuid "234cc714-ee95-51d3-9f60-96338562378e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70329641-1279-5076-9f37-fb06772be638" :answer/id #uuid "70329641-1279-5076-9f37-fb06772be638" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-15a967e4-1f67-5afa-8031-c76c4fbb09cf" :question/id #uuid "15a967e4-1f67-5afa-8031-c76c4fbb09cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-96263" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{5\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{5\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}(5\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, recall the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csch}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the above identity to express the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{csch}⁡x(5\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{csch}⁡x(5\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+3\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-33e72fa2-cc65-5b80-8195-b5d8928f38d2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-33e72fa2-cc65-5b80-8195-b5d8928f38d2" :answer-field/id #uuid "33e72fa2-cc65-5b80-8195-b5d8928f38d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3058b8fa-e6f3-593c-9d60-424339d2e4e9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3058b8fa-e6f3-593c-9d60-424339d2e4e9" "answer-bb8cb1aa-d2c5-5da0-96f0-51596aafbb34" "answer-44b1da90-8ca0-5d57-b272-29370ec5c888" "answer-037ba1f6-bab8-5644-a9f9-1d0997895160" "answer-05a68fca-8c3b-59b9-b009-99d530c3e80c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3058b8fa-e6f3-593c-9d60-424339d2e4e9" :answer/id #uuid "3058b8fa-e6f3-593c-9d60-424339d2e4e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+3\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb8cb1aa-d2c5-5da0-96f0-51596aafbb34" :answer/id #uuid "bb8cb1aa-d2c5-5da0-96f0-51596aafbb34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{csch}⁡x-3\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44b1da90-8ca0-5d57-b272-29370ec5c888" :answer/id #uuid "44b1da90-8ca0-5d57-b272-29370ec5c888" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+3\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-037ba1f6-bab8-5644-a9f9-1d0997895160" :answer/id #uuid "037ba1f6-bab8-5644-a9f9-1d0997895160" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+3\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05a68fca-8c3b-59b9-b009-99d530c3e80c" :answer/id #uuid "05a68fca-8c3b-59b9-b009-99d530c3e80c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sech}⁡x-3\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ee29c156-d06d-572b-b229-09cda1e3a6dc" :question/id #uuid "ee29c156-d06d-572b-b229-09cda1e3a6dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-352915" :question/problem "$$\n\nEvaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x}{2{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x}{2{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {coth}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow we need to find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the trigonometric identity \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the above identity to write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {coth}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{csch}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-1}-\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{5}{3}-\\frac{5}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3eb4c32a-3d20-50c8-8f9e-4bb89fd9ad7c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3eb4c32a-3d20-50c8-8f9e-4bb89fd9ad7c" :answer-field/id #uuid "3eb4c32a-3d20-50c8-8f9e-4bb89fd9ad7c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-36b11b91-37c1-568c-9d1a-8a39694f67a8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-36b11b91-37c1-568c-9d1a-8a39694f67a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36b11b91-37c1-568c-9d1a-8a39694f67a8" :answer/id #uuid "36b11b91-37c1-568c-9d1a-8a39694f67a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{24}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9fa8b923-c944-5ab9-8f5d-a280f219b3bf" :question/id #uuid "9fa8b923-c944-5ab9-8f5d-a280f219b3bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-352916" :question/problem "$$\n\nEvaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{tanh}^{2}⁡x}{2{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{tanh}^{2}⁡x}{2{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {tanh}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow we need to find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the trigonometric identity \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the above identity to write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {tanh}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{sech}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+1}-\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{3}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-241e61f4-57a8-5907-834c-7042fc78b039"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-241e61f4-57a8-5907-834c-7042fc78b039" :answer-field/id #uuid "241e61f4-57a8-5907-834c-7042fc78b039" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1fcdb4ad-14d5-5f0f-bf9e-41acc5a1d22e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1fcdb4ad-14d5-5f0f-bf9e-41acc5a1d22e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1fcdb4ad-14d5-5f0f-bf9e-41acc5a1d22e" :answer/id #uuid "1fcdb4ad-14d5-5f0f-bf9e-41acc5a1d22e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f7758d7e-a5ba-50ee-a45d-ff68b3cc6226" :question/id #uuid "f7758d7e-a5ba-50ee-a45d-ff68b3cc6226" :question/math-academy-id "q-352968" :question/problem "$$\n\nEvaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{coth}⁡x}{{csch}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identities that correspond to the following trigonometric identities:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identities are\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{csch}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{coth}⁡x}{{csch}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{csch}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\cdot {sinh}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\frac{5}{3}$ |\n\nNow, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{5/3}u\\,\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}{|}_{1}^{5/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({(\\frac{5}{3})}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{25}{9}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{9}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4af736d1-f000-5f15-b738-443b7520d5c7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4af736d1-f000-5f15-b738-443b7520d5c7" :answer-field/id #uuid "4af736d1-f000-5f15-b738-443b7520d5c7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2a2b669f-2579-5335-819c-e77eab944787" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2a2b669f-2579-5335-819c-e77eab944787"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a2b669f-2579-5335-819c-e77eab944787" :answer/id #uuid "2a2b669f-2579-5335-819c-e77eab944787" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7d070173-586a-5be7-bd5c-a4be4b18eeea" :question/id #uuid "7d070173-586a-5be7-bd5c-a4be4b18eeea" :question/math-academy-id "q-352966" :question/problem "$$\n\nEvaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}2\\operatorname{csch}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identities that correspond to the following trigonometric identities:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identities are\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{csch}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}2\\operatorname{csch}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\operatorname{csch}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=2x.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡16$ |\n\nNow, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}2{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\operatorname{csch}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡16}\\operatorname{csch}⁡(u)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(u)\\,\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csch}⁡(u){|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡16} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csch}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡16)+\\operatorname{csch}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡16)}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(\\frac{16-{16}^{-1}}{2})}+\\frac{1}{(\\frac{4-{4}^{-1}}{2})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(\\frac{255}{32})}+\\frac{1}{(\\frac{15}{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{104}{255}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-59c3d70b-5195-5774-847f-b546cbff6162"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-59c3d70b-5195-5774-847f-b546cbff6162" :answer-field/id #uuid "59c3d70b-5195-5774-847f-b546cbff6162" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-036a64a0-313e-560e-a52e-dc6b8481224c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-036a64a0-313e-560e-a52e-dc6b8481224c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-036a64a0-313e-560e-a52e-dc6b8481224c" :answer/id #uuid "036a64a0-313e-560e-a52e-dc6b8481224c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{104}{255}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b4fa5f6e-c8a3-5731-a2a2-6fc871183cc3" :question/id #uuid "b4fa5f6e-c8a3-5731-a2a2-6fc871183cc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-97309" :question/problem "$$\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2}}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following trigonometric identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2}}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2}}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2}$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ | $\\frac{4}{3}$ |\n\nNow, we evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2}}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{3/4}^{4/3}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{3/4}^{4/3}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{3/4}^{4/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4002135c-7d30-54e3-97cb-3c714ed2683f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4002135c-7d30-54e3-97cb-3c714ed2683f" :answer-field/id #uuid "4002135c-7d30-54e3-97cb-3c714ed2683f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4b6e5545-ad9f-555a-83ad-2208b3d8fb3f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7d7c2265-44f1-5e96-9940-d8c787667e23" "answer-57ae105c-8d7c-5650-bab1-27e1f5494f13" "answer-62f42da6-b448-5558-a669-efbc711b9a8c" "answer-371ed2b5-3cfd-5f36-ad25-78277503bf11" "answer-4b6e5545-ad9f-555a-83ad-2208b3d8fb3f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d7c2265-44f1-5e96-9940-d8c787667e23" :answer/id #uuid "7d7c2265-44f1-5e96-9940-d8c787667e23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{8}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57ae105c-8d7c-5650-bab1-27e1f5494f13" :answer/id #uuid "57ae105c-8d7c-5650-bab1-27e1f5494f13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62f42da6-b448-5558-a669-efbc711b9a8c" :answer/id #uuid "62f42da6-b448-5558-a669-efbc711b9a8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-371ed2b5-3cfd-5f36-ad25-78277503bf11" :answer/id #uuid "371ed2b5-3cfd-5f36-ad25-78277503bf11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b6e5545-ad9f-555a-83ad-2208b3d8fb3f" :answer/id #uuid "4b6e5545-ad9f-555a-83ad-2208b3d8fb3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8879f5ec-f2c2-51de-a1ef-edc8baad4b56" :question/id #uuid "8879f5ec-f2c2-51de-a1ef-edc8baad4b56" :question/math-academy-id "q-96498" :question/problem "$\\int {sech}^{4}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nFirst, recall the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the above identity and rewrite the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sech}^{4}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{4}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{4}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3{u}^{3}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3{cosh}^{3}⁡x}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}{sech}^{3}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d71d4fa5-c4c0-5c1e-bcc7-f6ccd2a9c51a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d71d4fa5-c4c0-5c1e-bcc7-f6ccd2a9c51a" :answer-field/id #uuid "d71d4fa5-c4c0-5c1e-bcc7-f6ccd2a9c51a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ec738ce0-bbfd-546f-8829-537d42455730" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3076c98e-4b5f-5295-a960-def6c68868a2" "answer-ec738ce0-bbfd-546f-8829-537d42455730" "answer-d05d1a37-cbd0-5beb-a2c1-20973dce818c" "answer-951bf2e0-4ba8-5e1e-9dc3-e53cb361313b" "answer-790e9e20-c3f7-5319-bd5c-6ff1a8086450"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3076c98e-4b5f-5295-a960-def6c68868a2" :answer/id #uuid "3076c98e-4b5f-5295-a960-def6c68868a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}{csch}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec738ce0-bbfd-546f-8829-537d42455730" :answer/id #uuid "ec738ce0-bbfd-546f-8829-537d42455730" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}{sech}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d05d1a37-cbd0-5beb-a2c1-20973dce818c" :answer/id #uuid "d05d1a37-cbd0-5beb-a2c1-20973dce818c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}{sech}^{4}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-951bf2e0-4ba8-5e1e-9dc3-e53cb361313b" :answer/id #uuid "951bf2e0-4ba8-5e1e-9dc3-e53cb361313b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{csch}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-790e9e20-c3f7-5319-bd5c-6ff1a8086450" :answer/id #uuid "790e9e20-c3f7-5319-bd5c-6ff1a8086450" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{sech}^{4}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-390d417d-9926-5446-a159-d0e16ff521f1" :question/id #uuid "390d417d-9926-5446-a159-d0e16ff521f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-138954" :question/problem "$$\n\n${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identities that correspond to the following trigonometric identities:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identities are\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{csch}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x})}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{{sinh}^{3}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ | $\\frac{4}{3}$ |\n\nNow, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{{sinh}^{3}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{3/4}^{4/3}\\frac{1}{{u}^{3}}\\,\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3/4}^{4/3}{u}^{-3}\\,\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{u}^{-3+1}}{-3+1}\\,{|}_{3/4}^{4/3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{u}^{2}}\\,{|}_{3/4}^{4/3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{(\\frac{4}{3})}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{32}+\\frac{8}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{175}{288}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7e082909-a6e2-55c2-a4a7-4878e06b14ff"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7e082909-a6e2-55c2-a4a7-4878e06b14ff" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e082909-a6e2-55c2-a4a7-4878e06b14ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-575e949f-a2b7-5302-ade7-234c593749f2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-575e949f-a2b7-5302-ade7-234c593749f2" "answer-84f09ef6-af8c-5278-868c-878e38fd43f7" "answer-e4be4b9f-6f9d-51ae-b85e-355d75cde324" "answer-94da350d-d600-5d09-a5e8-a507d6bea83a" "answer-9f8049a3-094e-56a7-a9bb-cd14ccc9b2ae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-575e949f-a2b7-5302-ade7-234c593749f2" :answer/id #uuid "575e949f-a2b7-5302-ade7-234c593749f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{175}{288}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84f09ef6-af8c-5278-868c-878e38fd43f7" :answer/id #uuid "84f09ef6-af8c-5278-868c-878e38fd43f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{175}{36}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4be4b9f-6f9d-51ae-b85e-355d75cde324" :answer/id #uuid "e4be4b9f-6f9d-51ae-b85e-355d75cde324" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{243}{64}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94da350d-d600-5d09-a5e8-a507d6bea83a" :answer/id #uuid "94da350d-d600-5d09-a5e8-a507d6bea83a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{35}{288}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f8049a3-094e-56a7-a9bb-cd14ccc9b2ae" :answer/id #uuid "9f8049a3-094e-56a7-a9bb-cd14ccc9b2ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{35}{36}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186168117 :tutorial/content "It's possible to convert every trigonometric identity to a corresponding *hyperbolic* identity using **Osborn's rule.** \n\nTo apply Osborn's rule, we follow two steps:\n\n1\\. Replace every trigonometric function with its corresponding hyperbolic function.\n\n2\\. For any product of *two trigonometric sines*, change the sign of the corresponding product of hyperbolic sines.\n\nTo demonstrate, consider the Pythagorean trigonometric identity:\n\n$$\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\cosh}{\\mathop{\\rm cosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sinh}{\\mathop{\\rm sinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\cos^2 x \\:{\\color{blue}{\\boldsymbol +}}\\: \\sin^2 x = 1\n$$\n\nNotice that this trigonometric identity contains a product of two sines. Therefore, to find the corresponding hyperbolic identity, we change each trigonometric function to its corresponding hyperbolic counterpart and change the sign in front of the corresponding product of sines. \n\nThus, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is\n\n$$\n\\cosh^2 x \\:{\\color{red}{\\boldsymbol -}}\\: \\sinh^2 x = 1.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe can check that this identity is indeed true using the definitions of the hyperbolic sine and cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x & ={(\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}))}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}))}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}{({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})}^{2}-{({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2x}+2+{e}^{-2x}-({e}^{2x}-2+{e}^{-2x})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\cancel{{e}^{2x}}+2+\\cancel{{e}^{-2x}}-(\\cancel{{e}^{2x}}-2+\\cancel{{e}^{-2x}})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186168153 :tutorial/content "When applying Osborn's rule, we must be aware that sometimes a product of two sines is \"hidden.\"\n\nTo demonstrate, consider the following trigonometric identity:\n\n$$\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\cosh}{\\mathop{\\rm cosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sinh}{\\mathop{\\rm sinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n1 \\:{\\color{blue}{\\boldsymbol +}}\\: \\tan^2 x = \\sec^2 x\n$$\n\nAt first glance, it may seem that there is no product of sines, and we do not need to change any signs in the corresponding hyperbolic identity.\n\nHowever, recall that\n\n$$\n\\tan x = \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n\\tan^2 x = \\dfrac{\\sin^2 x}{\\cos^2 x}.\n$$\n\nSo, there is a hidden product of sines within the $\\tan^2 x$ term, and we need to flip the sign in front of this term when writing down the corresponding hyperbolic identity.\n\nThus, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is\n\n$$\n1 \\:{\\color{red}{\\boldsymbol -}}\\: \\tanh^2 x = \\sech^2 x.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186168152 :tutorial/content "Suppose we want to calculate the integral\n\n$$\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sinh^2 x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nFirst, we note the following hyperbolic identity:\n\n$$\n\\csch{x} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sinh{x}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sinh^2{x}} \\,\\textrm{d}x\n= \\int \\left(\\dfrac{1}{\\sinh{x}}\\right)^2 \\,\\textrm{d}x\n= \\int \\csch^2{x} \\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nFrom here, we can see that this is just a standard hyperbolic integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sinh^2{x}}\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\int \\csch^2{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x = -\\coth{x} + C\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167026 :activity/expected-seconds 1380.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167732 :step/math-academy-id 631334 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167804 :step/math-academy-id 631335 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167761 :step/math-academy-id 631336 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167803 :step/math-academy-id 631339 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167626 :step/math-academy-id 631340 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167627 :step/math-academy-id 631343 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167628 :step/math-academy-id 631346 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186072620 :answer-field/choices 17592186072624] [:db/retract 17592186072620 :answer-field/choices 17592186072625] [:db/retract 17592186072620 :answer-field/choices 17592186072621] [:db/retract 17592186072620 :answer-field/choices 17592186072622] [:db/retract 17592186072620 :answer-field/choices 17592186072623] {:db/id 17592186054839 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8fef57fc-2f55-531e-87c9-45485e34049e" "question-23eee6bd-a3f3-5d31-99a2-293051ea115d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8fef57fc-2f55-531e-87c9-45485e34049e" :question/id #uuid "8fef57fc-2f55-531e-87c9-45485e34049e" :question/math-academy-id "q-179536" :question/problem "If $r=4,$ then $\\frac{2r}{3}-2=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Replacing $r$ with $4$ in the expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2r}{3}-2 & = \\\\ \\frac{2(4)}{3}-2 & = \\\\ \\frac{8}{3}-2 & = \\\\ \\frac{8-3\\cdot 2}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ec396184-e874-5ee9-9738-287768ca0067"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ec396184-e874-5ee9-9738-287768ca0067" :answer-field/id #uuid "ec396184-e874-5ee9-9738-287768ca0067" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-471a4b7a-98d9-5684-a4fb-e5881f1be8ed" :answer-field/choices ["answer-471a4b7a-98d9-5684-a4fb-e5881f1be8ed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-471a4b7a-98d9-5684-a4fb-e5881f1be8ed" :answer/id #uuid "471a4b7a-98d9-5684-a4fb-e5881f1be8ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129112 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a728363a-21de-5465-8925-c66dae64d6b5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a728363a-21de-5465-8925-c66dae64d6b5" :question/id #uuid "a728363a-21de-5465-8925-c66dae64d6b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-68624" :question/problem "${(-6\\times 9)}^{8}=$" :question/worked-solution "To raise the product of two numbers to the power of $8$, we can raise each number to the power of $8,$ and then multiply:\n\n$$\n{(-6\\times 9)}^{8}={((-6)\\times 9)}^{8}={(-6)}^{8}\\times {9}^{8}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-73f4611d-4e45-5ccf-b1af-13b6c55051a0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-73f4611d-4e45-5ccf-b1af-13b6c55051a0" :answer-field/id #uuid "73f4611d-4e45-5ccf-b1af-13b6c55051a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-50f85b86-e9ba-59a8-b2da-9a51e00908b6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-87f8d63b-e09b-5724-8eba-0a7230f34c23" "answer-072a18ed-0692-57cf-b3f4-7c7e022a388b" "answer-5cd6ad67-ba59-5cb2-a4ff-e07cdaa16ff0" "answer-50f85b86-e9ba-59a8-b2da-9a51e00908b6" "answer-eb0807e7-e82d-5da5-9889-3223730ef0a2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87f8d63b-e09b-5724-8eba-0a7230f34c23" :answer/id #uuid "87f8d63b-e09b-5724-8eba-0a7230f34c23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-6)\\times {9}^{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-072a18ed-0692-57cf-b3f4-7c7e022a388b" :answer/id #uuid "072a18ed-0692-57cf-b3f4-7c7e022a388b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\times {9}^{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5cd6ad67-ba59-5cb2-a4ff-e07cdaa16ff0" :answer/id #uuid "5cd6ad67-ba59-5cb2-a4ff-e07cdaa16ff0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(-6)}^{8}\\times 9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-50f85b86-e9ba-59a8-b2da-9a51e00908b6" :answer/id #uuid "50f85b86-e9ba-59a8-b2da-9a51e00908b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(-6)}^{8}\\times {9}^{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb0807e7-e82d-5da5-9889-3223730ef0a2" :answer/id #uuid "eb0807e7-e82d-5da5-9889-3223730ef0a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(\\frac{1}{6})}^{8}\\times {9}^{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138394 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8bf7e480-fb51-579e-b130-139151e7ecc4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8bf7e480-fb51-579e-b130-139151e7ecc4" :question/id #uuid "8bf7e480-fb51-579e-b130-139151e7ecc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-68992" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}}=$" :question/worked-solution "The square root of a quotient of two positive numbers is equal to the quotient of the square roots of the numbers. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{6}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-02aa50d8-7e59-5ec3-baec-32c35fa91223"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-02aa50d8-7e59-5ec3-baec-32c35fa91223" :answer-field/id #uuid "02aa50d8-7e59-5ec3-baec-32c35fa91223" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b68eee8c-221b-58d9-95b5-d015aa6fa3b2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d5a72cad-24d0-5be3-9016-0f236bf8df17" "answer-63e7d7b2-6328-5a7c-9e7b-fa3dbce3eabb" "answer-9667e35e-f889-55cd-8df1-5a84f2a0d662" "answer-f6c3fe8d-00a3-53be-a31e-4a67a046510c" "answer-b68eee8c-221b-58d9-95b5-d015aa6fa3b2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5a72cad-24d0-5be3-9016-0f236bf8df17" :answer/id #uuid "d5a72cad-24d0-5be3-9016-0f236bf8df17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{\\sqrt{6}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63e7d7b2-6328-5a7c-9e7b-fa3dbce3eabb" :answer/id #uuid "63e7d7b2-6328-5a7c-9e7b-fa3dbce3eabb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{6}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9667e35e-f889-55cd-8df1-5a84f2a0d662" :answer/id #uuid "9667e35e-f889-55cd-8df1-5a84f2a0d662" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{30}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6c3fe8d-00a3-53be-a31e-4a67a046510c" :answer/id #uuid "f6c3fe8d-00a3-53be-a31e-4a67a046510c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b68eee8c-221b-58d9-95b5-d015aa6fa3b2" :answer/id #uuid "b68eee8c-221b-58d9-95b5-d015aa6fa3b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{6}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152297 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-32edbf40-91ab-5dc2-911c-42534beb5cff"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-32edbf40-91ab-5dc2-911c-42534beb5cff" :question/id #uuid "32edbf40-91ab-5dc2-911c-42534beb5cff" :question/math-academy-id "q-318354" :question/problem "What number is $175%$ greater than $48?$" :question/worked-solution "To find a number $175%$ *greater than* $48,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+175%=275%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n275%=\\frac{275}{100}=2.75\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $175%$ greater than $48,$ we multiply $48$ by $2.75:$\n\n$$\n2.75\\cdot 48=132\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number that is $175%$ greater than $48$ is $132.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-98df2e4f-b683-5bb4-8a2e-794e7d7efd73"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-98df2e4f-b683-5bb4-8a2e-794e7d7efd73" :answer-field/id #uuid "98df2e4f-b683-5bb4-8a2e-794e7d7efd73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9647ff7c-56ee-5eaa-b169-213ba236e2d9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b97144c0-81e0-5543-82e8-e60b900bad57" "answer-5f957550-490c-5d15-93b3-98e6be45e35b" "answer-a0177ecd-9269-57dd-ac6c-b48ee7ad95ff" "answer-9647ff7c-56ee-5eaa-b169-213ba236e2d9" "answer-4c122ba6-cc81-5732-b3b3-5c73d49cce35"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b97144c0-81e0-5543-82e8-e60b900bad57" :answer/id #uuid "b97144c0-81e0-5543-82e8-e60b900bad57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "110" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f957550-490c-5d15-93b3-98e6be45e35b" :answer/id #uuid "5f957550-490c-5d15-93b3-98e6be45e35b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "120" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0177ecd-9269-57dd-ac6c-b48ee7ad95ff" :answer/id #uuid "a0177ecd-9269-57dd-ac6c-b48ee7ad95ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "125" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9647ff7c-56ee-5eaa-b169-213ba236e2d9" :answer/id #uuid "9647ff7c-56ee-5eaa-b169-213ba236e2d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "132" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c122ba6-cc81-5732-b3b3-5c73d49cce35" :answer/id #uuid "4c122ba6-cc81-5732-b3b3-5c73d49cce35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "140" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119768 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8b3fdd80-83cc-5d53-85c1-0216b4942139"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8b3fdd80-83cc-5d53-85c1-0216b4942139" :question/id #uuid "8b3fdd80-83cc-5d53-85c1-0216b4942139" :question/math-academy-id "q-33226" :question/problem "$3{w}^{4}-{w}^{3}-5{w}^{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $3{w}^{3}$ and $-5{w}^{3}$are like terms, so we group them, and then we add or subtract the coefficients.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{w}^{4}-{w}^{3}-5{w}^{4} & = \\\\ (3{w}^{4}-5{w}^{4})-{w}^{3} & = \\\\ (3-5){w}^{4}-{w}^{3} & = \\\\ -2{w}^{4}-{w}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c4f49a27-fbe6-5211-9e4e-77c7312508de"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c4f49a27-fbe6-5211-9e4e-77c7312508de" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4f49a27-fbe6-5211-9e4e-77c7312508de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-231fa41e-7562-58c3-bc53-a8af642e063c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d3ee0861-9665-55bd-98e5-b09f0500d4c5" "answer-231fa41e-7562-58c3-bc53-a8af642e063c" "answer-fd9c33f9-8e43-5ba3-8d78-df3475ffcd16" "answer-52e7dc11-9cb1-5f72-b61c-ed22849bf163" "answer-8f86123d-e422-5dce-9146-cf89e8645b54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3ee0861-9665-55bd-98e5-b09f0500d4c5" :answer/id #uuid "d3ee0861-9665-55bd-98e5-b09f0500d4c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{w}^{4}-5{w}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-231fa41e-7562-58c3-bc53-a8af642e063c" :answer/id #uuid "231fa41e-7562-58c3-bc53-a8af642e063c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{w}^{4}-{w}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd9c33f9-8e43-5ba3-8d78-df3475ffcd16" :answer/id #uuid "fd9c33f9-8e43-5ba3-8d78-df3475ffcd16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{w}^{4}-5{w}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52e7dc11-9cb1-5f72-b61c-ed22849bf163" :answer/id #uuid "52e7dc11-9cb1-5f72-b61c-ed22849bf163" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{w}^{4}-6{w}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f86123d-e422-5dce-9146-cf89e8645b54" :answer/id #uuid "8f86123d-e422-5dce-9146-cf89e8645b54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{w}^{4}-{w}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138388 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8f0c5a6d-560b-5b20-a886-377893e98cd2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8f0c5a6d-560b-5b20-a886-377893e98cd2" :question/id #uuid "8f0c5a6d-560b-5b20-a886-377893e98cd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-154082" :question/problem "The mass $m$ of a tablet PC measures $314.7\\,\\text{g}$ to the nearest tenth of a gram. Determine the upper and lower bounds of this measurement." :question/worked-solution "Our measurement is given to the nearest $0.1\\,\\text{g}.$ So, the greatest possible error of this measurement is\n\n$$\n\\frac{0.1\\,\\text{g}}{2}=0.05\\,\\text{g}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the lower and upper bounds of this measurement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{lower bound} & =314.7\\,\\text{g}-0.05\\,\\text{g} \\\\  & =314.65\\,\\text{g} \\\\ \\text{upper bound} & =314.7\\,\\text{g}+0.05\\,\\text{g} \\\\  & =314.75\\,\\text{g}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the exact value of $m$ lies between the lower and upper bound, we conclude that\n\n$$\n314.65\\,\\text{g}\\le m<314.75\\,\\text{g}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6435960d-f51a-52e7-94e7-a76e47e9ec99"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6435960d-f51a-52e7-94e7-a76e47e9ec99" :answer-field/id #uuid "6435960d-f51a-52e7-94e7-a76e47e9ec99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-fi