:knowledge-point/questions ["question-83ed0f7d-e76a-53b6-8cf6-264c24acad16" "question-0a6becce-61cc-5b53-a5ff-f772c9293a84" "question-d9fc617a-f5be-5a74-8545-9128626b78b2" "question-d62141b5-a243-5a9b-bfab-d11b88f8be6e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096629 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fe245032-d155-5a02-8475-f1836177bbab" "question-21c1c6c9-f8f1-50f1-a9ef-3d13b0e5c684" "question-2bcca121-9116-5327-93c6-12a3a1649264" "question-3994f797-7a6e-5428-aacb-fe36a9051f76"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-83ed0f7d-e76a-53b6-8cf6-264c24acad16" :question/id #uuid "83ed0f7d-e76a-53b6-8cf6-264c24acad16" :question/math-academy-id "q-73139" :question/problem "![](images/17/17f6b2ab535408802ef2776eea2db41ac20b17f3568e245ee87b13f05767203f.png)\n\nThe area under the curve $y=\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}$ between $x=0$, $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a left Riemann sum, as shown above. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" :question/worked-solution "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=3$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=3,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-0}{3}=\\frac{3}{3}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})Δx & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f(a+kΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{3-1}f(0+k\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}f(k) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}\\sqrt{9-{k}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-61f4da89-3768-5682-9582-88618e04b971"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-61f4da89-3768-5682-9582-88618e04b971" :answer-field/id #uuid "61f4da89-3768-5682-9582-88618e04b971" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e2bc2c15-5ae4-5cc7-8401-515b22401c82" :answer-field/choices ["answer-06c395f8-cf42-52aa-a803-43591ce1552c" "answer-9d636130-3c2c-52dd-9e9b-3376ca8624c2" "answer-e2bc2c15-5ae4-5cc7-8401-515b22401c82" "answer-fab745cb-883b-50ae-b463-3c48ccdfe0a3" "answer-57c77a3f-a887-515d-9a85-dfc4702748fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06c395f8-cf42-52aa-a803-43591ce1552c" :answer/id #uuid "06c395f8-cf42-52aa-a803-43591ce1552c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}\\sqrt{1-{k}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d636130-3c2c-52dd-9e9b-3376ca8624c2" :answer/id #uuid "9d636130-3c2c-52dd-9e9b-3376ca8624c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}\\sqrt{8-{k}^{2}-2k}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2bc2c15-5ae4-5cc7-8401-515b22401c82" :answer/id #uuid "e2bc2c15-5ae4-5cc7-8401-515b22401c82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}\\sqrt{9-{k}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fab745cb-883b-50ae-b463-3c48ccdfe0a3" :answer/id #uuid "fab745cb-883b-50ae-b463-3c48ccdfe0a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{k=0}^{3}\\sqrt{6-{k}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57c77a3f-a887-515d-9a85-dfc4702748fe" :answer/id #uuid "57c77a3f-a887-515d-9a85-dfc4702748fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{k=0}^{3}\\sqrt{8-{k}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0a6becce-61cc-5b53-a5ff-f772c9293a84" :question/id #uuid "0a6becce-61cc-5b53-a5ff-f772c9293a84" :question/math-academy-id "q-73069" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ between $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a left Riemann sum using $4$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" :question/worked-solution "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're given that $n=4$ subintervals.  The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0)}{4}=\\frac{\\pi }{8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{4-1}f(0+j\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{3}f(\\frac{j\\pi }{8})\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{3}\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f9b02b04-3990-5647-8a7e-f4a0b6db0f71"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f9b02b04-3990-5647-8a7e-f4a0b6db0f71" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9b02b04-3990-5647-8a7e-f4a0b6db0f71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5479d04f-11d8-52ff-a10f-c5daf44d5b8d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4cc7096b-e4d0-5551-8b4c-698c994185de" "answer-5479d04f-11d8-52ff-a10f-c5daf44d5b8d" "answer-d48e153e-cc47-599d-abb7-f430aae869da" "answer-79aff7b5-6b64-51d5-8c15-e972a08c75b0" "answer-30c148ce-3d4b-5f82-be22-94b1b7a941d5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4cc7096b-e4d0-5551-8b4c-698c994185de" :answer/id #uuid "4cc7096b-e4d0-5551-8b4c-698c994185de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5479d04f-11d8-52ff-a10f-c5daf44d5b8d" :answer/id #uuid "5479d04f-11d8-52ff-a10f-c5daf44d5b8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{8})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d48e153e-cc47-599d-abb7-f430aae869da" :answer/id #uuid "d48e153e-cc47-599d-abb7-f430aae869da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{8})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79aff7b5-6b64-51d5-8c15-e972a08c75b0" :answer/id #uuid "79aff7b5-6b64-51d5-8c15-e972a08c75b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30c148ce-3d4b-5f82-be22-94b1b7a941d5" :answer/id #uuid "30c148ce-3d4b-5f82-be22-94b1b7a941d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{8})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097271 :question/problem "![](images/35/35b881e8bb04eb192967ebc94945850fb0450012675369facd4efb41c611aaab.png)\n\nThe area under the curve $y=\\sqrt{x}$ between $x=1$, $x=4$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a left Riemann sum, as shown above. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" :question/worked-solution "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=3$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=1$ and $b=4,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-1}{3}=\\frac{3}{3}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=0}^{3-1}f(1+i\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=0}^{2}f(i+1) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=0}^{2}\\sqrt{i+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186095550 :answer-field/correct "answer-fb121efb-f9e3-53b8-983a-b475b7803a85" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fb121efb-f9e3-53b8-983a-b475b7803a85" "answer-c4de2e59-74dc-5cf4-9fcb-a0a43b5dac86" "answer-cc5ee95f-0280-530e-bb69-7f936cd23797" "answer-b9a457ee-275f-5ec7-a5b0-1ffb26f9cc22" "answer-c5f9bf07-ae92-50c1-ab4e-b76d5bf6aefd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb121efb-f9e3-53b8-983a-b475b7803a85" :answer/id #uuid "fb121efb-f9e3-53b8-983a-b475b7803a85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{i=0}^{2}\\sqrt{i+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4de2e59-74dc-5cf4-9fcb-a0a43b5dac86" :answer/id #uuid "c4de2e59-74dc-5cf4-9fcb-a0a43b5dac86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{i=0}^{2}\\sqrt{i+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc5ee95f-0280-530e-bb69-7f936cd23797" :answer/id #uuid "cc5ee95f-0280-530e-bb69-7f936cd23797" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{i=0}^{2}\\sqrt{i-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9a457ee-275f-5ec7-a5b0-1ffb26f9cc22" :answer/id #uuid "b9a457ee-275f-5ec7-a5b0-1ffb26f9cc22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{i=0}^{2}\\sqrt{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5f9bf07-ae92-50c1-ab4e-b76d5bf6aefd" :answer/id #uuid "c5f9bf07-ae92-50c1-ab4e-b76d5bf6aefd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}\\sqrt{i+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d9fc617a-f5be-5a74-8545-9128626b78b2" :question/id #uuid "d9fc617a-f5be-5a74-8545-9128626b78b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-49383" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=5-{x}^{2}$ between $x=-1$ and $x=1$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a left Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" :question/worked-solution "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of subintervals, ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$, and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nThe endpoints indicate that $a=-1$ and $b=1,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{1-(-1)}{n}=\\frac{2}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(-1+j\\cdot \\frac{2}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(-1+\\frac{2j}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[5-{(-1+\\frac{2j}{n})}^{2}]\\frac{2}{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\frac{2}{n}(4+\\frac{4j}{n}-\\frac{4{j}^{2}}{{n}^{2}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a4c4f8a5-a724-5fb9-9af0-afee36d1582d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a4c4f8a5-a724-5fb9-9af0-afee36d1582d" :answer-field/id #uuid "a4c4f8a5-a724-5fb9-9af0-afee36d1582d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-36b76477-1bee-5cfd-af35-4972e78ad218" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2cf153cd-dbf3-5f7a-9e7a-e147bed59a38" "answer-36b76477-1bee-5cfd-af35-4972e78ad218" "answer-1ab988cf-5693-58a8-b278-e05c02100c50" "answer-83db7859-91ab-56dc-83ce-dbb89d1f2482" "answer-f7fd2c5c-cf9d-5138-8ac5-87eba6bf55c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2cf153cd-dbf3-5f7a-9e7a-e147bed59a38" :answer/id #uuid "2cf153cd-dbf3-5f7a-9e7a-e147bed59a38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=0}^{1}\\frac{2}{n}(5-\\frac{4j}{n}+\\frac{4{j}^{2}}{{n}^{2}})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36b76477-1bee-5cfd-af35-4972e78ad218" :answer/id #uuid "36b76477-1bee-5cfd-af35-4972e78ad218" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\frac{2}{n}(4+\\frac{4j}{n}-\\frac{4{j}^{2}}{{n}^{2}})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ab988cf-5693-58a8-b278-e05c02100c50" :answer/id #uuid "1ab988cf-5693-58a8-b278-e05c02100c50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n}\\frac{2}{n}(4-\\frac{4j}{n}+\\frac{4{j}^{2}}{n})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83db7859-91ab-56dc-83ce-dbb89d1f2482" :answer/id #uuid "83db7859-91ab-56dc-83ce-dbb89d1f2482" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n}\\frac{2}{n}(5-\\frac{4{j}^{2}}{{n}^{2}})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7fd2c5c-cf9d-5138-8ac5-87eba6bf55c1" :answer/id #uuid "f7fd2c5c-cf9d-5138-8ac5-87eba6bf55c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\frac{2}{n}(\\frac{4j}{n}-\\frac{4{j}^{2}}{{n}^{2}})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d62141b5-a243-5a9b-bfab-d11b88f8be6e" :question/id #uuid "d62141b5-a243-5a9b-bfab-d11b88f8be6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-345028" :question/problem "![](images/7d/7d7a51344b945f502ace0aa7b9d5dee46514a465adda7666d83fe91bd2ffb3a2.png)\n\nThe area under the curve $y=\\sqrt{x+1}$ between $x=0$, $x=4$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a left Riemann sum, as shown above. What is the expression for the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $k.$*\n\n${S}_{L}={\\sum }_{k=0}^{3}$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=4$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=4,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-0}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})Δx & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f(a+kΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{4-1}f(0+k\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{3}f(k) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{3}\\sqrt{1+k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0cfdfcb5-7c50-5afa-92b2-1f208f863466"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0cfdfcb5-7c50-5afa-92b2-1f208f863466" :answer-field/id #uuid "0cfdfcb5-7c50-5afa-92b2-1f208f863466" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b0e29592-9ea2-5a39-a74f-62ec0996efbc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b0e29592-9ea2-5a39-a74f-62ec0996efbc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0e29592-9ea2-5a39-a74f-62ec0996efbc" :answer/id #uuid "b0e29592-9ea2-5a39-a74f-62ec0996efbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{k+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fe245032-d155-5a02-8475-f1836177bbab" :question/id #uuid "fe245032-d155-5a02-8475-f1836177bbab" :question/math-academy-id "q-315710" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+1)$ between $x=-1$ and $x=2$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $j$ and $n.$*\n\n${S}_{R}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\frac{3}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡($\n{{field-1}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're told that there are $n$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=-1$ and $b=2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{2-(-1)}{n}=\\frac{3}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[f(-1+j\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{3}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(-1+\\frac{3j}{n})+1)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\frac{3}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{6j}{n}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-da4b8589-0630-5be5-bada-40a46902ce0a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-da4b8589-0630-5be5-bada-40a46902ce0a" :answer-field/id #uuid "da4b8589-0630-5be5-bada-40a46902ce0a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-4f0daa64-ab0d-5c7d-bc74-4d0c2bf2920a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4f0daa64-ab0d-5c7d-bc74-4d0c2bf2920a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f0daa64-ab0d-5c7d-bc74-4d0c2bf2920a" :answer/id #uuid "4f0daa64-ab0d-5c7d-bc74-4d0c2bf2920a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6j}{n}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-21c1c6c9-f8f1-50f1-a9ef-3d13b0e5c684" :question/id #uuid "21c1c6c9-f8f1-50f1-a9ef-3d13b0e5c684" :question/math-academy-id "q-116626" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=\\sqrt{x+2}$ between $x=-2$ and $x=2$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $7$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is   \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're told that there are $n=7$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=-2$ and $b=2.$ So, the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{2-(-2)}{7}=\\frac{4}{7}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}f(-2+i\\cdot \\frac{4}{7})\\cdot \\frac{4}{7} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}f(-2+\\frac{4i}{7})\\cdot \\frac{4}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\,\\sqrt{(-2+\\frac{4i}{7})+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{4i}{7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3ee4b5b3-c121-55ee-96bd-54041a866832"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3ee4b5b3-c121-55ee-96bd-54041a866832" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ee4b5b3-c121-55ee-96bd-54041a866832" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-af0d5166-e6c8-504d-975f-ece6f9efdfce" :answer-field/choices ["answer-43b8f5fb-30a4-58cc-b827-a3c6c0f1627e" "answer-af0d5166-e6c8-504d-975f-ece6f9efdfce" "answer-12436895-69cb-503c-8085-217ca08ec281" "answer-4eec80dc-bf63-5e26-a70a-c9df0a844d2d" "answer-d6cf2865-18ea-59ba-9dab-3d90e49f0104"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43b8f5fb-30a4-58cc-b827-a3c6c0f1627e" :answer/id #uuid "43b8f5fb-30a4-58cc-b827-a3c6c0f1627e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{2i}{7}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af0d5166-e6c8-504d-975f-ece6f9efdfce" :answer/id #uuid "af0d5166-e6c8-504d-975f-ece6f9efdfce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{4i}{7}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12436895-69cb-503c-8085-217ca08ec281" :answer/id #uuid "12436895-69cb-503c-8085-217ca08ec281" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{i}{7}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4eec80dc-bf63-5e26-a70a-c9df0a844d2d" :answer/id #uuid "4eec80dc-bf63-5e26-a70a-c9df0a844d2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{4i}{7}+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6cf2865-18ea-59ba-9dab-3d90e49f0104" :answer/id #uuid "d6cf2865-18ea-59ba-9dab-3d90e49f0104" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\,i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2bcca121-9116-5327-93c6-12a3a1649264" :question/id #uuid "2bcca121-9116-5327-93c6-12a3a1649264" :question/math-academy-id "q-345038" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=(x+1)^{2}$ between $x=-1$ and $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $4$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $i.$*\n\n${S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is   \n\n$$\n{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're told that there are $n=4$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=-1$ and $b=3.$ So, the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-(-1)}{4}=\\frac{4}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(-1+i\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(-1+i)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}\\,{(-1+i+1)}^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}\\,{i}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-07fff1fe-7a31-59f7-8640-95363928e02e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-07fff1fe-7a31-59f7-8640-95363928e02e" :answer-field/id #uuid "07fff1fe-7a31-59f7-8640-95363928e02e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-cf9c4b37-e372-57d7-a0be-33097ed1ca8b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cf9c4b37-e372-57d7-a0be-33097ed1ca8b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf9c4b37-e372-57d7-a0be-33097ed1ca8b" :answer/id #uuid "cf9c4b37-e372-57d7-a0be-33097ed1ca8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3994f797-7a6e-5428-aacb-fe36a9051f76" :question/id #uuid "3994f797-7a6e-5428-aacb-fe36a9051f76" :question/math-academy-id "q-49364" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ between $x=0$ and $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're told that there are $n$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-0}{n}=\\frac{3}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[f(0+j\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[f(\\frac{3j}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{3}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3j}{n})].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4a1a980a-9817-5cc2-b963-bee9f053f5b9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4a1a980a-9817-5cc2-b963-bee9f053f5b9" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a1a980a-9817-5cc2-b963-bee9f053f5b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-242d5a8d-320a-55dd-af45-50bb63662fa4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-16912225-3f70-5541-b574-3061e2e7b38e" "answer-761dcd9a-706c-5db6-a6b8-883ea8047a63" "answer-9b62e5a4-9e97-5400-851f-d6ea027be307" "answer-242d5a8d-320a-55dd-af45-50bb63662fa4" "answer-e1d1bf4f-0539-5436-aeaf-4b61a267639b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16912225-3f70-5541-b574-3061e2e7b38e" :answer/id #uuid "16912225-3f70-5541-b574-3061e2e7b38e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{3n})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-761dcd9a-706c-5db6-a6b8-883ea8047a63" :answer/id #uuid "761dcd9a-706c-5db6-a6b8-883ea8047a63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3j}{n})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b62e5a4-9e97-5400-851f-d6ea027be307" :answer/id #uuid "9b62e5a4-9e97-5400-851f-d6ea027be307" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{2}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2j}{n})]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-242d5a8d-320a-55dd-af45-50bb63662fa4" :answer/id #uuid "242d5a8d-320a-55dd-af45-50bb63662fa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{3}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3j}{n})]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1d1bf4f-0539-5436-aeaf-4b61a267639b" :answer/id #uuid "e1d1bf4f-0539-5436-aeaf-4b61a267639b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{j}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096850 :activity/expected-seconds 840.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162096 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b9e3535a-6a10-557b-a90a-dcbee5f059a0" "question-6a4bb009-1382-5d80-b122-5cf6749f1552"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b9e3535a-6a10-557b-a90a-dcbee5f059a0" :question/id #uuid "b9e3535a-6a10-557b-a90a-dcbee5f059a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-138608" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & ⋯ & {x}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis given by \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & ⋯ & {b}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${b}_{i}={x}_{i}-m$ for $i=1,2,…,n,$ and $m$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 21\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9980a067-163c-5305-b9d5-aeb44a51e2ee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9980a067-163c-5305-b9d5-aeb44a51e2ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "9980a067-163c-5305-b9d5-aeb44a51e2ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ad6e45b4-0d19-5a65-9da0-878c4f37d052" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4e278261-12a2-522a-865f-2ee4f991690d" "answer-95c87fe0-b27d-523b-b97f-283a3892f373" "answer-c4625cbc-5b19-59bd-9eb5-2085cc809466" "answer-ad6e45b4-0d19-5a65-9da0-878c4f37d052" "answer-c24f6fe3-8f3b-5e4f-87ee-cd603ef7bb00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e278261-12a2-522a-865f-2ee4f991690d" :answer/id #uuid "4e278261-12a2-522a-865f-2ee4f991690d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95c87fe0-b27d-523b-b97f-283a3892f373" :answer/id #uuid "95c87fe0-b27d-523b-b97f-283a3892f373" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4625cbc-5b19-59bd-9eb5-2085cc809466" :answer/id #uuid "c4625cbc-5b19-59bd-9eb5-2085cc809466" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad6e45b4-0d19-5a65-9da0-878c4f37d052" :answer/id #uuid "ad6e45b4-0d19-5a65-9da0-878c4f37d052" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c24f6fe3-8f3b-5e4f-87ee-cd603ef7bb00" :answer/id #uuid "c24f6fe3-8f3b-5e4f-87ee-cd603ef7bb00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6a4bb009-1382-5d80-b122-5cf6749f1552" :question/id #uuid "6a4bb009-1382-5d80-b122-5cf6749f1552" :question/math-academy-id "q-138615" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & ⋯ & {x}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis given by \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & ⋯ & {b}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${b}_{i}={x}_{i}-m$ for $i=1,2,…,n,$ and $m$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b518b34a-8d6e-54eb-93d9-d3cb5a0505b0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b518b34a-8d6e-54eb-93d9-d3cb5a0505b0" :answer-field/id #uuid "b518b34a-8d6e-54eb-93d9-d3cb5a0505b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bfecac8a-fa87-5d62-a946-7f122c1e66c9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bfecac8a-fa87-5d62-a946-7f122c1e66c9" "answer-581f54a2-60c9-5dc5-bb4d-f8f318fe2d6f" "answer-7a4429f4-c191-50e8-be52-084fe635f47b" "answer-f1218c8e-974e-52d6-b624-68fd43f78159" "answer-57509c8b-6b98-51aa-9762-9963caf04358"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bfecac8a-fa87-5d62-a946-7f122c1e66c9" :answer/id #uuid "bfecac8a-fa87-5d62-a946-7f122c1e66c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-581f54a2-60c9-5dc5-bb4d-f8f318fe2d6f" :answer/id #uuid "581f54a2-60c9-5dc5-bb4d-f8f318fe2d6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a4429f4-c191-50e8-be52-084fe635f47b" :answer/id #uuid "7a4429f4-c191-50e8-be52-084fe635f47b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1218c8e-974e-52d6-b624-68fd43f78159" :answer/id #uuid "f1218c8e-974e-52d6-b624-68fd43f78159" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57509c8b-6b98-51aa-9762-9963caf04358" :answer/id #uuid "57509c8b-6b98-51aa-9762-9963caf04358" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162095 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5926666e-0db3-5dee-9762-40fbc13f71e2" "question-2f2cb4c0-5e13-5762-90d1-d095feb4a65e" "question-d39bfe0e-e6e3-509a-9ccb-2651e206d7a8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5926666e-0db3-5dee-9762-40fbc13f71e2" :question/id #uuid "5926666e-0db3-5dee-9762-40fbc13f71e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-138627" :question/problem "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $B$ in the mean-deviation form above, where the individual observations are given in columns. \nFind the sample covariance matrix of the data." :question/worked-solution "Recall that  the sample covariance matrix is given by\n\n$$\nC=\\frac{1}{n-1}B{B}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is the observation matrix in the mean-deviation form, and $n$ is the number of observations.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\frac{1}{4-1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 42\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fef71c07-ba83-5d64-938a-f5aa72763b99"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fef71c07-ba83-5d64-938a-f5aa72763b99" :answer-field/id #uuid "fef71c07-ba83-5d64-938a-f5aa72763b99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f3949942-a93b-5278-9bdf-682422d7e809" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f3949942-a93b-5278-9bdf-682422d7e809" "answer-99ee16dd-f5ce-5d55-9f57-ac836de565b8" "answer-2c32cbe8-c57b-5bf3-a19d-03d660a7ac0a" "answer-4ba53bf9-6d2f-55fc-bcb0-4c3a502a927e" "answer-a35b201c-f9c8-5ef5-99f4-35d4c0535194"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3949942-a93b-5278-9bdf-682422d7e809" :answer/id #uuid "f3949942-a93b-5278-9bdf-682422d7e809" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 42\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99ee16dd-f5ce-5d55-9f57-ac836de565b8" :answer/id #uuid "99ee16dd-f5ce-5d55-9f57-ac836de565b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -27\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c32cbe8-c57b-5bf3-a19d-03d660a7ac0a" :answer/id #uuid "2c32cbe8-c57b-5bf3-a19d-03d660a7ac0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}34 & -17 \\\\ -17 & -29\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ba53bf9-6d2f-55fc-bcb0-4c3a502a927e" :answer/id #uuid "4ba53bf9-6d2f-55fc-bcb0-4c3a502a927e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}34 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -29\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a35b201c-f9c8-5ef5-99f4-35d4c0535194" :answer/id #uuid "a35b201c-f9c8-5ef5-99f4-35d4c0535194" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}46 & 77 \\\\ 77 & 21\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2f2cb4c0-5e13-5762-90d1-d095feb4a65e" :question/id #uuid "2f2cb4c0-5e13-5762-90d1-d095feb4a65e" :question/math-academy-id "q-138631" :question/problem "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 10 & -6 & 5 & -9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $B$ in the mean-deviation form above, where the individual observations are given in columns. \nFind the sample covariance matrix of the data." :question/worked-solution "Recall that  the sample covariance matrix is given by\n\n$$\nC=\\frac{1}{n-1}B{B}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is the observation matrix in the mean-deviation form, and $n$ is the number of observations.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\frac{1}{4-1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 10 & -6 & 5 & -9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 10 \\\\ 5 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}62 & -69 \\\\ -69 & 242\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-677e14b0-94a5-52de-a477-ccd697d060de"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-677e14b0-94a5-52de-a477-ccd697d060de" :answer-field/id #uuid "677e14b0-94a5-52de-a477-ccd697d060de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-313c180d-6683-5895-8319-1cc5e1d0047d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3528ecab-4caa-5dc2-8341-f72254cce85e" "answer-ff8daa35-c661-577d-b35d-32e5b20ab32b" "answer-4c4801ac-f3c0-54c9-9d9b-068066aba1b3" "answer-313c180d-6683-5895-8319-1cc5e1d0047d" "answer-551ede1c-3223-5e2a-a363-e21869ad5829"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3528ecab-4caa-5dc2-8341-f72254cce85e" :answer/id #uuid "3528ecab-4caa-5dc2-8341-f72254cce85e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}25 & -25 \\\\ -25 & 47\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff8daa35-c661-577d-b35d-32e5b20ab32b" :answer/id #uuid "ff8daa35-c661-577d-b35d-32e5b20ab32b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}30 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 69\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c4801ac-f3c0-54c9-9d9b-068066aba1b3" :answer/id #uuid "4c4801ac-f3c0-54c9-9d9b-068066aba1b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}52 & 30 \\\\ 30 & 250\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-313c180d-6683-5895-8319-1cc5e1d0047d" :answer/id #uuid "313c180d-6683-5895-8319-1cc5e1d0047d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}62 & -69 \\\\ -69 & 242\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-551ede1c-3223-5e2a-a363-e21869ad5829" :answer/id #uuid "551ede1c-3223-5e2a-a363-e21869ad5829" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}65 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 340\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d39bfe0e-e6e3-509a-9ccb-2651e206d7a8" :question/id #uuid "d39bfe0e-e6e3-509a-9ccb-2651e206d7a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-138639" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the sample covariance matrix of the data." :question/worked-solution "Recall that  the sample covariance matrix is given by\n\n$$\nC=\\frac{1}{n-1}B{B}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is the observation matrix in the mean-deviation form, and $n$ is the number of observations.\n\nSo, we first need to compute the mean-deviation form of our observation matrix.\n\nThe sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the sample covariance matrix is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\frac{1}{3-1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 42\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-63610fdd-4a0f-5e58-8e91-40c9b79c1b2f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-63610fdd-4a0f-5e58-8e91-40c9b79c1b2f" :answer-field/id #uuid "63610fdd-4a0f-5e58-8e91-40c9b79c1b2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5f060f18-5f38-57d0-8035-ee521e1efa10" :answer-field/choices ["answer-63f36174-881c-57cb-888e-5b635ad28017" "answer-6a9c88b3-2c09-54a3-99c5-91c575160cb4" "answer-82ed669f-a9bd-5e1c-8760-9d608342f7c3" "answer-5f060f18-5f38-57d0-8035-ee521e1efa10" "answer-e3398816-b77b-5ead-950a-9a70459413a7"] :db/ensure [:a