n-b9e3535a-6a10-557b-a90a-dcbee5f059a0" :step/next "step-c3d9e78e-168e-5b62-9c51-d4a45ca0bbdb" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c3d9e78e-168e-5b62-9c51-d4a45ca0bbdb" :step/id #uuid "c3d9e78e-168e-5b62-9c51-d4a45ca0bbdb" :step/content "question-6a4bb009-1382-5d80-b122-5cf6749f1552" :step/next "step-0346e43f-4ec3-54fd-a36a-83c457ba540d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0346e43f-4ec3-54fd-a36a-83c457ba540d" :step/id #uuid "0346e43f-4ec3-54fd-a36a-83c457ba540d" :step/content "question-5926666e-0db3-5dee-9762-40fbc13f71e2" :step/next "step-23e83d25-72e7-5ce0-8291-4514123ca24b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-23e83d25-72e7-5ce0-8291-4514123ca24b" :step/id #uuid "23e83d25-72e7-5ce0-8291-4514123ca24b" :step/content "question-2f2cb4c0-5e13-5762-90d1-d095feb4a65e" :step/next "step-d14ef892-c3d1-5aad-87b3-30b8a9ceff03" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d14ef892-c3d1-5aad-87b3-30b8a9ceff03" :step/id #uuid "d14ef892-c3d1-5aad-87b3-30b8a9ceff03" :step/content "question-d39bfe0e-e6e3-509a-9ccb-2651e206d7a8" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186173704 :answer-field/choices 17592186173705] [:db/retract 17592186173704 :answer-field/choices 17592186173706] [:db/retract 17592186173704 :answer-field/choices 17592186173707] [:db/retract 17592186173704 :answer-field/choices 17592186173708] [:db/retract 17592186173704 :answer-field/choices 17592186173709] {:db/id 17592186092374 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-50970995-9b99-52ed-ae6b-c20b930d578c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-50970995-9b99-52ed-ae6b-c20b930d578c" :question/id #uuid "50970995-9b99-52ed-ae6b-c20b930d578c" :question/math-academy-id "q-9537" :question/problem "![](images/50/5034bb902aadd151cc1a28764e054dbdd6a694ad653f50557e5fc208c8ec2342.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi $ (shown in blue in the diagram above).\n\n*Hint: You may wish to use the following identity: $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}.$*" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall the identity for $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}):$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}\n$$\n\nUsing $x=\\theta $ in the above identity, the integral can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={2\\cdot 2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2}))|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =4(1-0) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e6fa46cf-d1f0-5fd4-a76c-c62db6438a9c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e6fa46cf-d1f0-5fd4-a76c-c62db6438a9c" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6fa46cf-d1f0-5fd4-a76c-c62db6438a9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-725bc856-b7c0-56dc-9518-bdc1f5428c77" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f6d4553a-62e1-59c9-8854-5587cc1e9c71" "answer-cc05201a-8232-5a04-8ce3-e3ac354a9f76" "answer-2ada2e3d-0769-5b5a-85e6-218cbeec1c89" "answer-725bc856-b7c0-56dc-9518-bdc1f5428c77" "answer-4b33b710-8754-5317-ad8d-edc5c3f9305d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6d4553a-62e1-59c9-8854-5587cc1e9c71" :answer/id #uuid "f6d4553a-62e1-59c9-8854-5587cc1e9c71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc05201a-8232-5a04-8ce3-e3ac354a9f76" :answer/id #uuid "cc05201a-8232-5a04-8ce3-e3ac354a9f76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ada2e3d-0769-5b5a-85e6-218cbeec1c89" :answer/id #uuid "2ada2e3d-0769-5b5a-85e6-218cbeec1c89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-725bc856-b7c0-56dc-9518-bdc1f5428c77" :answer/id #uuid "725bc856-b7c0-56dc-9518-bdc1f5428c77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b33b710-8754-5317-ad8d-edc5c3f9305d" :answer/id #uuid "4b33b710-8754-5317-ad8d-edc5c3f9305d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147399 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d80dc7c0-9327-55d2-9040-e9261d08f05c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d80dc7c0-9327-55d2-9040-e9261d08f05c" :question/id #uuid "d80dc7c0-9327-55d2-9040-e9261d08f05c" :question/math-academy-id "q-349991" :question/problem "The total amount of money $M(t)$ in a charity’s fundraising account $t$ days after the first day of a campaign is given by the function\n\n$$\nM(t)=1500+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-27)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere $M$ is measured in dollars, and $t\\ge 0$ is the time (in days) since the first day of the campaign.\n\nFind the time when the total amount is minimum, and how much money was in the account at that time.\n\nThe minimum amount is\n$$$\n{{field-1}}\nafter \n{{field-2}} days." :question/worked-solution "To find when the total amount is a minimum, we need to solve $\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=0.$ First, we differentiate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1500+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-27)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1500)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-27)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-27)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we solve $\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=0$:\n\n$$\n3{t}^{2}-27=0\\,⇒\\,t=3\n$$\n\nSo there are two candidates for global extrema, $t=0$ and $t=3.$ To find out how much money is in the account when $t=3,$ we figure out $M(3)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M(3) & =1500+{\\int }_{0}^{3}(3{x}^{2}-27)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1500+[{x}^{3}-27x]{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =1500+[({3}^{3}-27(3))-(0)] \\\\  & =1500+[27-81] \\\\  & =1500-54 \\\\  & =1446\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $1446<1500$, we conclude that the minimum amount is $$\\,1446$, and this will happen after $3$ days." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a36923dd-8b5c-56f5-b238-c554200e0681" "answer-field-b20711af-5c25-5a71-ae61-9921ee570e17"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a36923dd-8b5c-56f5-b238-c554200e0681" :answer-field/id #uuid "a36923dd-8b5c-56f5-b238-c554200e0681" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-df50d26b-36b0-56c5-b8ab-6313ce61f333" :answer-field/choices ["answer-df50d26b-36b0-56c5-b8ab-6313ce61f333"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df50d26b-36b0-56c5-b8ab-6313ce61f333" :answer/id #uuid "df50d26b-36b0-56c5-b8ab-6313ce61f333" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1446" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b20711af-5c25-5a71-ae61-9921ee570e17" :answer-field/id #uuid "b20711af-5c25-5a71-ae61-9921ee570e17" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-15462584-19cb-5b6e-9995-3d3c0d41935d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-15462584-19cb-5b6e-9995-3d3c0d41935d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15462584-19cb-5b6e-9995-3d3c0d41935d" :answer/id #uuid "15462584-19cb-5b6e-9995-3d3c0d41935d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176241 :question/problem "![](images/58/5806f57e41eeb5548b0c041533adf3952dd7f35236121f9056c57f03c2854ddc.png)\n\nConsider the arc of the curve $y=\\sqrt{1-x}$ that lies in the first quadrant between $x=0$ and its $x$-intercept. What integral gives the area of the surface generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis?" :question/worked-solution "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi x\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $y=f(x),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}x\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we find where the curve intersects the $x$-axis by solving the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1-x} & =0 \\\\ 1-x & =0 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $x=0$ to $x=1.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{1-x})=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}x\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\sqrt{1+{(-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-x}})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4(1-x)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\sqrt{\\frac{5-4x}{4(1-x)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\sqrt{\\frac{4x-5}{x-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186173704 :answer-field/correct "answer-e52ce18d-55d4-5980-93b5-05d516aca7c5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d82f7750-cdb5-5af6-a415-d4526008d845" "answer-3ce04388-54d1-53d5-91e9-530b14e04a5d" "answer-e52ce18d-55d4-5980-93b5-05d516aca7c5" "answer-26347220-3d03-59ee-8e7b-cb61d02c8618" "answer-58346a39-6f7b-5629-aba6-151206e88d2d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d82f7750-cdb5-5af6-a415-d4526008d845" :answer/id #uuid "d82f7750-cdb5-5af6-a415-d4526008d845" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x-1}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ce04388-54d1-53d5-91e9-530b14e04a5d" :answer/id #uuid "3ce04388-54d1-53d5-91e9-530b14e04a5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\sqrt{\\frac{4x-7}{x-1}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e52ce18d-55d4-5980-93b5-05d516aca7c5" :answer/id #uuid "e52ce18d-55d4-5980-93b5-05d516aca7c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\sqrt{\\frac{4x-5}{x-1}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26347220-3d03-59ee-8e7b-cb61d02c8618" :answer/id #uuid "26347220-3d03-59ee-8e7b-cb61d02c8618" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{x-1}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58346a39-6f7b-5629-aba6-151206e88d2d" :answer/id #uuid "58346a39-6f7b-5629-aba6-151206e88d2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{4x-7}{x-1}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-dc0e234d-b992-588f-b6af-c684a6467dfa" :activity/id #uuid "dc0e234d-b992-588f-b6af-c684a6467dfa" :activity/title "Quiz 2" :activity/type :activity.type/assessment :activity/course 17592186046645 :activity/steps ["step-6658199f-07f8-5ee5-96c7-e1415acede8a" "step-5e6cf617-c728-543e-ba88-85418d553d8f" "step-d912ee93-2c60-59a8-8030-8b4cb9171afe" "step-a792d8fe-f954-5743-ab0d-63ffa1aac63c" "step-a82d7e6d-d029-58a5-adca-46793e317249"] :activity/first-step "step-6658199f-07f8-5ee5-96c7-e1415acede8a" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-6658199f-07f8-5ee5-96c7-e1415acede8a" :step/id #uuid "6658199f-07f8-5ee5-96c7-e1415acede8a" :step/content "question-50970995-9b99-52ed-ae6b-c20b930d578c" :step/next "step-5e6cf617-c728-543e-ba88-85418d553d8f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-5e6cf617-c728-543e-ba88-85418d553d8f" :step/id #uuid "5e6cf617-c728-543e-ba88-85418d553d8f" :step/content 17592186332814 :step/next "step-d912ee93-2c60-59a8-8030-8b4cb9171afe" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d912ee93-2c60-59a8-8030-8b4cb9171afe" :step/id #uuid "d912ee93-2c60-59a8-8030-8b4cb9171afe" :step/content "question-d80dc7c0-9327-55d2-9040-e9261d08f05c" :step/next "step-a792d8fe-f954-5743-ab0d-63ffa1aac63c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a792d8fe-f954-5743-ab0d-63ffa1aac63c" :step/id #uuid "a792d8fe-f954-5743-ab0d-63ffa1aac63c" :step/content 17592186176241 :step/next "step-a82d7e6d-d029-58a5-adca-46793e317249" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a82d7e6d-d029-58a5-adca-46793e317249" :step/id #uuid "a82d7e6d-d029-58a5-adca-46793e317249" :step/content 17592186253561 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055261 :question/problem "Evaluate $1+(2-3x)$ for $x=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "We replace $x$ with $-1$ in the expression and evaluate the parentheses first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+(2-3x) & = \\\\ 1+(2-3\\cdot (-1)) & = \\\\ 1+(2-(-3)) & = \\\\ 1+(2+3) & = \\\\ 1+5 & = \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186052803 :answer-field/correct 17592186052805 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054841 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f350f45b-6b40-5442-831e-bda149e4ff5d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f350f45b-6b40-5442-831e-bda149e4ff5d" :question/id #uuid "f350f45b-6b40-5442-831e-bda149e4ff5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-41203" :question/problem "If $p=2$ and $q=-2,$ then $8p+7q+2=$" :question/worked-solution "Replacing $p$ with $2$ and $q$ with $-2$ in the expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8p+7q+2 & = \\\\ 8(2)+7(-2)+2 & = \\\\ 16+(-14)+2 & = \\\\ 16-14+2 & = \\\\ 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bd06868d-23f4-5b1c-a48c-3253d06db7ac"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bd06868d-23f4-5b1c-a48c-3253d06db7ac" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd06868d-23f4-5b1c-a48c-3253d06db7ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ceffc3ea-0be6-5e49-bd61-93965c77fc7f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a3b3c01c-522f-573c-9eb2-ad4d95b6fe5d" "answer-aabb5221-9e59-59ad-89e3-cdfd40a76ef1" "answer-6d10c19e-e150-55eb-b24f-880c7b312823" "answer-ee0c7ef3-1224-563f-ab0a-0e9a6c26a9b3" "answer-ceffc3ea-0be6-5e49-bd61-93965c77fc7f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3b3c01c-522f-573c-9eb2-ad4d95b6fe5d" :answer/id #uuid "a3b3c01c-522f-573c-9eb2-ad4d95b6fe5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aabb5221-9e59-59ad-89e3-cdfd40a76ef1" :answer/id #uuid "aabb5221-9e59-59ad-89e3-cdfd40a76ef1" 