9806c7e93bb4b704a03284905d968869fa1b4146.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the kite above?\n\nI. $AB=AD.$\n\nII. The kite has a pair of congruent opposite angles.\n\nIII. $AB=BC=CD=AD.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. A kite is a quadrilateral with two pairs of congruent sides that are adjacent to each other. In the figure, we can see that $AB=AD.$\n\n- Statement II is true. A kite always has a pair of congruent opposite angles.\n\n- Statement III is false. A kite is a quadrilateral with two pairs of congruent sides that are adjacent to each other. However, not all sides are congruent, for instance, $AB\\ne BC.$\n\nIn conclusion, statements I and II are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6a514638-3f19-527b-a1de-1e926b7c8285"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6a514638-3f19-527b-a1de-1e926b7c8285" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a514638-3f19-527b-a1de-1e926b7c8285" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8d7da163-a580-5e50-a38f-f8e138ef74c7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8d7da163-a580-5e50-a38f-f8e138ef74c7" "answer-edec2c50-c3f2-5ae9-9a96-0ba69435f615" "answer-24387f91-25bf-5714-8675-ef415eba960e" "answer-f02da5b5-90ef-5511-90c7-04d4ca4bf833" "answer-28dbcf41-1538-5429-b8d5-50fbfa182de1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d7da163-a580-5e50-a38f-f8e138ef74c7" :answer/id #uuid "8d7da163-a580-5e50-a38f-f8e138ef74c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-edec2c50-c3f2-5ae9-9a96-0ba69435f615" :answer/id #uuid "edec2c50-c3f2-5ae9-9a96-0ba69435f615" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24387f91-25bf-5714-8675-ef415eba960e" :answer/id #uuid "24387f91-25bf-5714-8675-ef415eba960e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f02da5b5-90ef-5511-90c7-04d4ca4bf833" :answer/id #uuid "f02da5b5-90ef-5511-90c7-04d4ca4bf833" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28dbcf41-1538-5429-b8d5-50fbfa182de1" :answer/id #uuid "28dbcf41-1538-5429-b8d5-50fbfa182de1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-55788c3c-c1d0-5ef8-8ff4-5e5fd3b4c618" :question/id #uuid "55788c3c-c1d0-5ef8-8ff4-5e5fd3b4c618" :question/math-academy-id "q-53012" :question/problem "![](images/4e/4e20dca5a916c43e93dd94b92ff4c1949a111537a8cb2e45b9ca0be7e2300f40.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the square above?\n\nI. $AB=BC=CD=AD.$\n\nII. $m∠ABC=m∠ADC.$\n\nIII. $\\overset{―}{AD}$ is parallel to $\\overset{―}{BC}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. A square is a rectangle where all sides are congruent, hence $AB=BC=CD=AD.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The angles in a square are all right. Therefore, $m∠ABC={90}^{∘}=m∠ADC.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Opposite sides of a square are parallel, and $\\overset{―}{AD}$ is opposite $\\overset{―}{BC},$ therefore $\\overset{―}{AD}$ is parallel to $\\overset{―}{BC}.$\n\nIn conclusion, statements I, II, and III are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ec71a978-52b7-54a3-b5fa-ef72f160c9d6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ec71a978-52b7-54a3-b5fa-ef72f160c9d6" :answer-field/id #uuid "ec71a978-52b7-54a3-b5fa-ef72f160c9d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5af8d66e-d7ec-5f20-b9b6-13fb2ff0d05e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f5b0cf17-65c2-51ce-89a4-44437b972a52" "answer-48305576-11d5-5617-960a-a3990bcb7dca" "answer-5af8d66e-d7ec-5f20-b9b6-13fb2ff0d05e" "answer-bfbf47b7-c34e-5794-aa4d-102f253c4306" "answer-f2464b38-1ef3-59d6-af91-e21eb614b53f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5b0cf17-65c2-51ce-89a4-44437b972a52" :answer/id #uuid "f5b0cf17-65c2-51ce-89a4-44437b972a52" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48305576-11d5-5617-960a-a3990bcb7dca" :answer/id #uuid "48305576-11d5-5617-960a-a3990bcb7dca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5af8d66e-d7ec-5f20-b9b6-13fb2ff0d05e" :answer/id #uuid "5af8d66e-d7ec-5f20-b9b6-13fb2ff0d05e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bfbf47b7-c34e-5794-aa4d-102f253c4306" :answer/id #uuid "bfbf47b7-c34e-5794-aa4d-102f253c4306" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2464b38-1ef3-59d6-af91-e21eb614b53f" :answer/id #uuid "f2464b38-1ef3-59d6-af91-e21eb614b53f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186111263 :question/worked-solution "First, recall the hierarchy diagram of quadrilaterals, where each shape below another is a specific type of the one above it.\n\n![](images/1d/1dbe4c3e8ea97c0ac077c37143802366c5817d86965ab1dbc5abf54cd01d27c3.png)\n\nRemember that a parallelogram is a quadrilateral with $2$ pairs of parallel sides.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each shape in turn.\n\n- The shape $P$ is a rectangle. Therefore, its opposite sides are parallel, so it is a parallelogram.\n\n- The shape $Q$ is a kite. It has a pair of opposite sides that are not parallel, therefore, it is not a parallelogram.\n\n- The shape $R$ is a rhombus. Since the opposite sides of a rhombus are parallel, it is a parallelogram.\n\n- The shape $S$ is a trapezoid. It has only one pair of parallel sides, therefore, it is not a parallelogram.\n\nTherefore, shapes $P$ and $R$ are parallelograms. The shapes $Q$ and $S$ are not parallelograms." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186109303 :answer-field/correct 17592186109308 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "activity-5011f029-40b3-50ae-adc7-c8594e763c6a" :activity/id #uuid "5011f029-40b3-50ae-adc7-c8594e763c6a" :activity/title "Classifying Quadrilaterals" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049068 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-866cff26-8806-5fb7-acaa-154a2dd5266d" "step-6b24c0db-50fd-51da-9580-556fff1c0632" "step-2cfe7fe6-dfad-5186-856c-597f87ad3a5e"] :activity/first-step "step-866cff26-8806-5fb7-acaa-154a2dd5266d" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-866cff26-8806-5fb7-acaa-154a2dd5266d" :step/id #uuid "866cff26-8806-5fb7-acaa-154a2dd5266d" :step/content "question-13987c3a-59aa-55ed-8fe6-1cb169d96b89" :step/next "step-6b24c0db-50fd-51da-9580-556fff1c0632" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-6b24c0db-50fd-51da-9580-556fff1c0632" :step/id #uuid "6b24c0db-50fd-51da-9580-556fff1c0632" :step/content "question-55788c3c-c1d0-5ef8-8ff4-5e5fd3b4c618" :step/next "step-2cfe7fe6-dfad-5186-856c-597f87ad3a5e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2cfe7fe6-dfad-5186-856c-597f87ad3a5e" :step/id #uuid "2cfe7fe6-dfad-5186-856c-597f87ad3a5e" :step/content 17592186111263 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100943 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-aac8b725-2415-58f2-86b7-ef6ffd39cf4e" "question-d2dfce9f-843a-50f1-956d-65c7968632c5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-aac8b725-2415-58f2-86b7-ef6ffd39cf4e" :question/id #uuid "aac8b725-2415-58f2-86b7-ef6ffd39cf4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-83853" :question/problem "Which of the following differential equations is a logistic growth equation?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFrom the given options, the only logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=3y-4{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTo see this, let's factor the right-hand side of the equation. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=4y(\\frac{3}{4}-y).\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the constant of proportionality is $k=4,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=\\frac{3}{4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6fb6b47e-6d7c-543e-a3d2-2ef7185b7ec9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6fb6b47e-6d7c-543e-a3d2-2ef7185b7ec9" :answer-field/id #uuid "6fb6b47e-6d7c-543e-a3d2-2ef7185b7ec9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f5f817ac-4342-536d-890b-3ceed2d07931" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c19039df-bdb3-5ee3-9b88-548c6a17e19b" "answer-4c2e65ff-a8f3-5761-bf62-d366e3c46fca" "answer-0ba7e32a-043c-5931-9dab-fc2b20f12800" "answer-f5f817ac-4342-536d-890b-3ceed2d07931" "answer-7567addf-e4b0-589e-a11d-3a3a13e6546a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c19039df-bdb3-5ee3-9b88-548c6a17e19b" :answer/id #uuid "c19039df-bdb3-5ee3-9b88-548c6a17e19b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=3+y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c2e65ff-a8f3-5761-bf62-d366e3c46fca" :answer/id #uuid "4c2e65ff-a8f3-5761-bf62-d366e3c46fca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=3-{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ba7e32a-043c-5931-9dab-fc2b20f12800" :answer/id #uuid "0ba7e32a-043c-5931-9dab-fc2b20f12800" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=3y+{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5f817ac-4342-536d-890b-3ceed2d07931" :answer/id #uuid "f5f817ac-4342-536d-890b-3ceed2d07931" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=3y-4{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7567addf-e4b0-589e-a11d-3a3a13e6546a" :answer/id #uuid "7567addf-e4b0-589e-a11d-3a3a13e6546a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=4-y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100942 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8b4b9134-52af-5188-95f0-9a0da05afadf" "question-9f125700-0b98-51e1-a020-af8c1b00c96f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8b4b9134-52af-5188-95f0-9a0da05afadf" :question/id #uuid "8b4b9134-52af-5188-95f0-9a0da05afadf" :question/math-academy-id "q-83861" :question/problem "The growth rate of the crab population $P(t)$ in a certain lake is jointly proportional to the crab population at time $t,$ measured in years, and the difference between the lake's carrying capacity and the crab population. If the constant of proportionality is $0.05$ and the maximum possible crab population is $1\\,000,$ which differential equation could be used to model $P(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the crab population's growth rate is *jointly* proportional to the crab population at time $t$ and the difference between the carrying capacity and the crab population, the crab population follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.05,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=1\\,000.$ Therefore, the crab population is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.05P(1\\,000-P).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0175e659-cba3-56a0-ab48-25d20caff549"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0175e659-cba3-56a0-ab48-25d20caff549" :answer-field/id #uuid "0175e659-cba3-56a0-ab48-25d20caff549" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2cd7eaeb-5a1a-5699-bd57-bb98c1bd9464" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e0fceb3e-eb15-5178-8697-6df9c91f70e9" "answer-f2c768ba-28d5-5f1d-815a-361c780dab8c" "answer-2cd7eaeb-5a1a-5699-bd57-bb98c1bd9464" "answer-1bd23510-2db8-57da-b03b-19947512a51c" "answer-3a51bae9-e725-5a29-b29e-cc1f2c4e37c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0fceb3e-eb15-5178-8697-6df9c91f70e9" :answer/id #uuid "e0fceb3e-eb15-5178-8697-6df9c91f70e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=-0.05P(1\\,000+P)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2c768ba-28d5-5f1d-815a-361c780dab8c" :answer/id #uuid "f2c768ba-28d5-5f1d-815a-361c780dab8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.05P(1\\,000+P)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2cd7eaeb-5a1a-5699-bd57-bb98c1bd9464" :answer/id #uuid "2cd7eaeb-5a1a-5699-bd57-bb98c1bd9464" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.05P(1\\,000-P)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1bd23510-2db8-57da-b03b-19947512a51c" :answer/id #uuid "1bd23510-2db8-57da-b03b-19947512a51c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=1\\,000P(0.05+P)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a51bae9-e725-5a29-b29e-cc1f2c4e37c7" :answer/id #uuid "3a51bae9-e725-5a29-b29e-cc1f2c4e37c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dP}{dt}=1\\,000P(0.05-P)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d2dfce9f-843a-50f1-956d-65c7968632c5" :question/id #uuid "d2dfce9f-843a-50f1-956d-65c7968632c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-119272" :question/problem "Which of the following differential equations is a logistic growth equation?" :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFrom the given options, the only logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=12y-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTo see this, let's factor the right-hand side of the equation. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=\\frac{3}{2}y(8-y).\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the constant of proportionality is $k=\\frac{3}{2},$ and the carrying capacity is $a=8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5145867a-16a7-5938-9452-ce8785416418"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5145867a-16a7-5938-9452-ce8785416418" :answer-field/id #uuid "5145867a-16a7-5938-9452-ce8785416418" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ea474472-9aa6-58f8-92d7-2af3c1726240" :answer-field/choices ["answer-22b2c358-09d5-578e-8970-70cbd506ef07" "answer-a05d2a83-b19c-56b6-8c4a-abda407e4876" "answer-bb7ed10b-16fa-58b9-9d6f-f538691e80da" "answer-ea474472-9aa6-58f8-92d7-2af3c1726240" "answer-93d3472f-ebac-5e70-ab44-c478a48ef8a0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22b2c358-09d5-578e-8970-70cbd506ef07" :answer/id #uuid "22b2c358-09d5-578e-8970-70cbd506ef07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=12-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a05d2a83-b19c-56b6-8c4a-abda407e4876" :answer/id #uuid "a05d2a83-b19c-56b6-8c4a-abda407e4876" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=12y+\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb7ed10b-16fa-58b9-9d6f-f538691e80da" :answer/id #uuid "bb7ed10b-16fa-58b9-9d6f-f538691e80da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=12y-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea474472-9aa6-58f8-92d7-2af3c1726240" :answer/id #uuid "ea474472-9aa6-58f8-92d7-2af3c1726240" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=12y-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93d3472f-ebac-5e70-ab44-c478a48ef8a0" :answer/id #uuid "93d3472f-ebac-5e70-ab44-c478a48ef8a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9f125700-0b98-51e1-a020-af8c1b00c96f" :question/id #uuid "9f125700-0b98-51e1-a020-af8c1b00c96f" :question/math-academy-id "q-119285" :question/problem "The growth rate of the population $P(t)$ in a certain country is jointly proportional to the population at time $t,$ measured in years, and the difference between the country's carrying capacity and the population. If the constant of proportionality is $0.000\\,01$ and the maximum possible population is $30\\,000\\,000,$ which differential equation could be used to model $P(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the population's growth rate is *jointly* proportional to the population at time $t$ and the difference between the carrying capacity and the population, the population follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.000\\,01,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=30\\,000\\,000.$ Therefore, the population is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.000\\,01P(30\\,000\\,000-P).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-06e2caa6-684d-5873-b7d1-19bd4b554ff8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-06e2caa6-684d-5873-b7d1-19bd4b554ff8" :answer-field/id #uuid "06e2caa6-684d-5873-b7d1-19bd4b554ff8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b5633021-65b1-5655-851a-9c5cc3387aa0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-74e2b3d2-bce7-54a2-9b79-91471f680491" "answer-c1b2688a-a907-53f7-9404-a7e6a7f57da7" "answer-b5633021-65b1-5655-851a-9c5cc3387aa0" "answer-9ff927fc-13bd-58f0-ae73-06ad00980ab2" "answer-743e3759-02ab-55f0-b4e0-a5e188a47db8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74e2b3d2-bce7-54a2-9b79-91471f680491" :answer/id #uuid "74e2b3d2-bce7-54a2-9b79-91471f680491" :answer/type :answer.ty