b/id "activity-884db384-9de1-557a-84a4-3a3f0a422a85" :activity/id #uuid "884db384-9de1-557a-84a4-3a3f0a422a85" :activity/title "Constructing a Taylor Polynomial Using a Graph, Estimating Functions, and the Alternating Series Error Bound" :activity/type :activity.type/assignment :activity/steps ["step-848fd617-c737-54e6-85bd-c49cba43ccd4"] :activity/first-step "step-848fd617-c737-54e6-85bd-c49cba43ccd4" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-848fd617-c737-54e6-85bd-c49cba43ccd4" :step/id #uuid "848fd617-c737-54e6-85bd-c49cba43ccd4" :step/content "assigned-problem-51de3932-d411-58ac-b226-f2b9dcd0fc96" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204008 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3b535844-eddd-540b-a454-365555c2e28f" "question-e546cbd8-6c28-59cf-9108-41c070e316fd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204010 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5cbb4944-93ba-5c18-a003-1720623144e5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3b535844-eddd-540b-a454-365555c2e28f" :question/id #uuid "3b535844-eddd-540b-a454-365555c2e28f" :question/math-academy-id "q-251875" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $5$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $5$ | $8$ | $9$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $7$ | $9$ |\n\nCalculate ${S}_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their respective means, that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample means $\\overset{―}{x}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{5+8+9+5+6}{5}=6.6\n$$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{8+9+10+7+9}{5}=8.6\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the ${x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{x}$, ${y}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}$, and their product.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $5$ | $8$ | $9$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $7$ | $9$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})\\,$** | $-1.6$ | $1.4$ | $2.4$ | $-1.6$ | $-0.6$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $-0.6$ | $0.4$ | $1.4$ | $-1.6$ | $0.4$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $0.96$ | $0.56$ | $3.36$ | $2.56$ | $-0.24$ |\n\nTherefore, ${S}_{xy}$ is\n\n$$\n{S}_{xy}=0.96+0.56+3.36+2.56+(-0.24)=7.2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9d05e707-cf16-5915-a547-c70d2c206fee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9d05e707-cf16-5915-a547-c70d2c206fee" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d05e707-cf16-5915-a547-c70d2c206fee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-47de3422-ffeb-5a17-b14f-74498ea093ca" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ee5147e7-4d0d-55e3-9a32-5af3e4b874b2" "answer-47de3422-ffeb-5a17-b14f-74498ea093ca" "answer-f1f5c552-e8d5-558d-8758-dda8b1d41492" "answer-d3e6e201-f276-5cd8-881c-e11c2c1e59c2" "answer-7d408cf0-77ba-54f6-afce-3f39ab3ef960"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee5147e7-4d0d-55e3-9a32-5af3e4b874b2" :answer/id #uuid "ee5147e7-4d0d-55e3-9a32-5af3e4b874b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=6.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47de3422-ffeb-5a17-b14f-74498ea093ca" :answer/id #uuid "47de3422-ffeb-5a17-b14f-74498ea093ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=7.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1f5c552-e8d5-558d-8758-dda8b1d41492" :answer/id #uuid "f1f5c552-e8d5-558d-8758-dda8b1d41492" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=7.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3e6e201-f276-5cd8-881c-e11c2c1e59c2" :answer/id #uuid "d3e6e201-f276-5cd8-881c-e11c2c1e59c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=9.0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d408cf0-77ba-54f6-afce-3f39ab3ef960" :answer/id #uuid "7d408cf0-77ba-54f6-afce-3f39ab3ef960" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=9.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e546cbd8-6c28-59cf-9108-41c070e316fd" :question/id #uuid "e546cbd8-6c28-59cf-9108-41c070e316fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-251876" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $7$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $1.2$ | $1.0$ | $0.7$ | $1.3$ | $1.8$ | $1.7$ | $1.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $6.6$ | $6.1$ | $5.7$ | $6.0$ | $6.3$ | $5.9$ | $5.4$ |\n\nCalculate ${S}_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their respective means, that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample means $\\overset{―}{x}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1.2+1.0+0.7+1.3+1.8+1.4+1.7}{7}=1.3\n$$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{6.6+6.1+5.7+6.0+6.3+5.9+5.4}{7}=6\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the ${x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{x}$, ${y}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}$, and their product.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $1.2$ | $1.0$ | $0.7$ | $1.3$ | $1.8$ | $1.7$ | $1.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $6.6$ | $6.1$ | $5.7$ | $6.0$ | $6.3$ | $5.9$ | $5.4$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})\\,$** | $-0.1$ | $-0.3$ | $-0.6$ | $0$ | $0.5$ | $0.4$ | $0.1$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $0.6$ | $0.1$ | $-0.3$ | $0$ | $0.3$ | $-0.1$ | $-0.6$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $-0.06$ | $-0.03$ | $0.18$ | $0$ | $0.15$ | $-0.04$ | $-0.06$ |\n\nTherefore, ${S}_{xy}$ is\n\n$$\n{S}_{xy}=(-0.06)+(-0.03)+0.18+0+0.15+(-0.04)+(-0.06)=0.14.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5b37bc23-4463-5cf2-acb2-e2f4162f0ffc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5b37bc23-4463-5cf2-acb2-e2f4162f0ffc" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b37bc23-4463-5cf2-acb2-e2f4162f0ffc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-87b37972-f264-5fe7-be91-6532a22909a4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3a4e3e32-81eb-5215-b6e7-ca840cc59c2c" "answer-87b37972-f264-5fe7-be91-6532a22909a4" "answer-f0f966f8-f580-5c9c-9ccf-b3a48389f82a" "answer-e2058f1c-ca6b-5704-b24a-ad1af833dee9" "answer-1f654eb5-da33-51e7-b9e3-237f2b57649d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a4e3e32-81eb-5215-b6e7-ca840cc59c2c" :answer/id #uuid "3a4e3e32-81eb-5215-b6e7-ca840cc59c2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=0.06" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87b37972-f264-5fe7-be91-6532a22909a4" :answer/id #uuid "87b37972-f264-5fe7-be91-6532a22909a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=0.14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0f966f8-f580-5c9c-9ccf-b3a48389f82a" :answer/id #uuid "f0f966f8-f580-5c9c-9ccf-b3a48389f82a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=1.12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2058f1c-ca6b-5704-b24a-ad1af833dee9" :answer/id #uuid "e2058f1c-ca6b-5704-b24a-ad1af833dee9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=1.33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f654eb5-da33-51e7-b9e3-237f2b57649d" :answer/id #uuid "1f654eb5-da33-51e7-b9e3-237f2b57649d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=2.80" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204448 :question/problem "Consider two sets of $25$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{25},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{25}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=125,\\,{S}_{yy}=37,\\,{S}_{xy}=64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, $Cov(x,y)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ their covariance can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their means.\n\nWe are given that ${S}_{xy}=64.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{64}{25} \\\\  & =2.56.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186202614 :answer-field/correct "answer-453923a5-93c8-5c6f-bfec-b6cdf2b78c6c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-453923a5-93c8-5c6f-bfec-b6cdf2b78c6c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-453923a5-93c8-5c6f-bfec-b6cdf2b78c6c" :answer/id #uuid "453923a5-93c8-5c6f-bfec-b6cdf2b78c6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.56" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5cbb4944-93ba-5c18-a003-1720623144e5" :question/id #uuid "5cbb4944-93ba-5c18-a003-1720623144e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-251837" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $27$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{27},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{27}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{27}{x}_{i}=540,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{27}{y}_{i}=567, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{27}{x}_{i}^{2}=12\\,050,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{27}{y}_{i}^{2}=14\\,107.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the sum of the squared deviations from the mean for the points ${x}_{i}.$\n\n${S}_{xx}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data ${x}_{i}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2}-\\frac{1}{n}{({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistics in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & =12\\,050-\\frac{1}{27}(540)^{2} \\\\  & =12\\,050-10\\,800 \\\\  & =1\\,250.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0ae99c74-d6dc-56f1-8e0e-a0b4df319323"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0ae99c74-d6dc-56f1-8e0e-a0b4df319323" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ae99c74-d6dc-56f1-8e0e-a0b4df319323" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e22bc458-30f2-56c5-a752-2720115543c5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e22bc458-30f2-56c5-a752-2720115543c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e22bc458-30f2-56c5-a752-2720115543c5" :answer/id #uuid "e22bc458-30f2-56c5-a752-2720115543c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1250" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233680 :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b96494db-5dd2-5488-8cf6-d406dbf495a4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b96494db-5dd2-5488-8cf6-d406dbf495a4" :answer-field/id #uuid "b96494db-5dd2-5488-8cf6-d406dbf495a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2032787c-d22e-592f-81df-10f4faf70894" :answer-field/choices ["answer-38df4399-89bc-529e-b1a6-df9d281a088f" "answer-9050f4d8-8c17-564c-9e1c-31ba36d7157b" "answer-2032787c-d22e-592f-81df-10f4faf70894" "answer-cfd589a9-8236-5537-bc1d-3196c955ccaf" "answer-6586d857-9cd0-591a-a6b4-187ac642b6a1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38df4399-89bc-529e-b1a6-df9d281a088f" :answer/id #uuid "38df4399-89bc-529e-b1a6-df9d281a088f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=21" :db/e