  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We want to express the area $A$ between the function $f(x)=4x-{x}^{2}$ and the $x$-axis, between $x=2$ and $x=4.$\n\nThis can be expressed as the definite integral of $f(x)=4x-{x}^{2}$ between the lower limit $x=2$ and the upper limit $x=4,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{2}^{4}4x-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-112aa2bb-1ece-5377-9ffe-f5b8c8a417d2" "answer-field-8f867861-bac8-5acd-9bcd-fa6e1eeaa057" "answer-field-353d24fe-51db-5000-8f6f-b37f521dedbb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-112aa2bb-1ece-5377-9ffe-f5b8c8a417d2" :answer-field/id #uuid "112aa2bb-1ece-5377-9ffe-f5b8c8a417d2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-48f6dc02-acc0-5810-a49a-8db847455a01" :answer-field/choices ["answer-48f6dc02-acc0-5810-a49a-8db847455a01"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48f6dc02-acc0-5810-a49a-8db847455a01" :answer/id #uuid "48f6dc02-acc0-5810-a49a-8db847455a01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8f867861-bac8-5acd-9bcd-fa6e1eeaa057" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f867861-bac8-5acd-9bcd-fa6e1eeaa057" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-54f3dfcf-2254-5bd5-81c8-3fa50ac7e058" :answer-field/choices ["answer-54f3dfcf-2254-5bd5-81c8-3fa50ac7e058"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54f3dfcf-2254-5bd5-81c8-3fa50ac7e058" :answer/id #uuid "54f3dfcf-2254-5bd5-81c8-3fa50ac7e058" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x-x^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-353d24fe-51db-5000-8f6f-b37f521dedbb" :answer-field/id #uuid "353d24fe-51db-5000-8f6f-b37f521dedbb" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-75537e4d-adc2-5a2a-854f-5e6551132e67" :answer-field/choices ["answer-75537e4d-adc2-5a2a-854f-5e6551132e67"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75537e4d-adc2-5a2a-854f-5e6551132e67" :answer/id #uuid "75537e4d-adc2-5a2a-854f-5e6551132e67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9b711075-e236-581f-bbc6-a977cb1be5c8" :question/id #uuid "9b711075-e236-581f-bbc6-a977cb1be5c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-113878" :question/problem "![](images/8b/8b242c0012bdbc048f350158333b78e9484d716aa44f28511df2d7126dd02098.png)\n\nFor the function $f(x)=\\frac{4x}{1+{x}^{2}}$ shown above, what is the expression for the area $A$ as a definite integral?" :question/worked-solution "We want to express the area $A$ between the function $f(x)=\\frac{4x}{1+{x}^{2}}$ and the $x$-axis, between $x=0$ and $x=3.$\n\nThis can be expressed as the definite integral of $f(x)=\\frac{4x}{1+{x}^{2}}$ between the lower limit $x=0$ and the upper limit $x=3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{4x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-203e8af7-bb35-5d46-9aaf-dc74ebadff71"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-203e8af7-bb35-5d46-9aaf-dc74ebadff71" :answer-field/id #uuid "203e8af7-bb35-5d46-9aaf-dc74ebadff71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-52ec8218-cb93-5d37-b283-4b9bd6f9587a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-912ffbe2-ddaf-5ff5-8704-c4428391999f" "answer-52ec8218-cb93-5d37-b283-4b9bd6f9587a" "answer-a0021d94-413d-51d9-9095-8420090359ad" "answer-aa06468b-d081-5ca0-9aa0-f0eefdcf9cdc" "answer-f16db77c-2e42-5645-bf9b-aef2827a8c45"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-912ffbe2-ddaf-5ff5-8704-c4428391999f" :answer/id #uuid "912ffbe2-ddaf-5ff5-8704-c4428391999f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A={\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\frac{4x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52ec8218-cb93-5d37-b283-4b9bd6f9587a" :answer/id #uuid "52ec8218-cb93-5d37-b283-4b9bd6f9587a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{4x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0021d94-413d-51d9-9095-8420090359ad" :answer/id #uuid "a0021d94-413d-51d9-9095-8420090359ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa06468b-d081-5ca0-9aa0-f0eefdcf9cdc" :answer/id #uuid "aa06468b-d081-5ca0-9aa0-f0eefdcf9cdc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f16db77c-2e42-5645-bf9b-aef2827a8c45" :answer/id #uuid "f16db77c-2e42-5645-bf9b-aef2827a8c45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186232933 :answer-field/correct "answer-103ab8d5-f369-5cfd-9868-b7b325f3ef49" :answer-field/choices ["answer-103ab8d5-f369-5cfd-9868-b7b325f3ef49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-103ab8d5-f369-5cfd-9868-b7b325f3ef49" :answer/id #uuid "103ab8d5-f369-5cfd-9868-b7b325f3ef49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x^2+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5a9d714c-fb16-5bf1-a044-d2aaa53f540d" :question/id #uuid "5a9d714c-fb16-5bf1-a044-d2aaa53f540d" :question/math-academy-id "q-346169" :question/problem "Express ${\\int }_{1}^{4}3{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x$ as the limit of a left Riemann sum.\n\n*Hint: Write down the missing expression in terms of $i$ and $n.$*\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{4}3{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[3($\n{{field-1}}\n$)^{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]$" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}3{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=3{x}^{3},$ the lower bound is $a=1,$ and the upper bound is $b=4.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-1}{n}=\\frac{3}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}3{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(1+i\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[3{(\\,1+\\frac{3i}{n}\\,)}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7d7e966e-716c-5603-9e5c-a619cf8a9b2c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7d7e966e-716c-5603-9e5c-a619cf8a9b2c" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d7e966e-716c-5603-9e5c-a619cf8a9b2c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ea371c3a-ee29-5549-a033-ba24d614dda7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ea371c3a-ee29-5549-a033-ba24d614dda7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea371c3a-ee29-5549-a033-ba24d614dda7" :answer/id #uuid "ea371c3a-ee29-5549-a033-ba24d614dda7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\frac{3i}{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-328da786-31ee-5734-9605-611059a862b9" :question/id #uuid "328da786-31ee-5734-9605-611059a862b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-346178" :question/problem "Express ${\\int }_{1}^{7}\\frac{2}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x$ as the limit of a left Riemann sum.\n\n*Hint: Write down the missing expression in terms of $i$ and $n.$*\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{7}\\frac{2}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\cdot \\frac{6}{n}]$" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{7}\\frac{2}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=\\frac{2}{x+3},$ the lower bound is $a=1,$ and the upper bound is $b=7.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{7-1}{n}=\\frac{6}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{7}\\frac{2}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(1+i\\cdot \\frac{6}{n})\\cdot \\frac{6}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(1+\\frac{6i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{6}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\frac{2}{(1+6i/n)+3}\\cdot \\frac{6}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[(\\frac{2}{6i/n+4})\\cdot \\frac{6}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[(\\,\\frac{1}{3i/n+2}\\,)\\cdot \\frac{6}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5d35b0bb-b5aa-56f8-b1ec-f3250b4039ff"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5d35b0bb-b5aa-56f8-b1ec-f3250b4039ff" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d35b0bb-b5aa-56f8-b1ec-f3250b4039ff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9b5bd4c2-f489-5064-969b-dfe5f50bb313" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9b5bd4c2-f489-5064-969b-dfe5f50bb313"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b5bd4c2-f489-5064-969b-dfe5f50bb313" :answer/id #uuid "9b5bd4c2-f489-5064-969b-dfe5f50bb313" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3i/n+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8aa630f2-bd34-5568-baf8-ea73abca85e8" :question/id #uuid "8aa630f2-bd34-5568-baf8-ea73abca85e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-73155" :question/problem "What is ${\\int }_{2}^{5}2{x}^{1/3}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{5}2{x}^{1/3}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=2{x}^{1/3},$ the lower bound is $a=2,$ and the upper bound is $b=5.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{5-2}{n}=\\frac{3}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{5}2{x}^{1/3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[f(2+j\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[f(2+\\frac{3j}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[2{(2+\\frac{3j}{n})}^{1/3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-057a26a6-55af-55a3-897b-914138a1eb9b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-057a26a6-55af-55a3-897b-914138a1eb9b" :answer-field/id #uuid "057a26a6-55af-55a3-897b-914138a1eb9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7d93b2a2-ea70-5d27-a06b-2eb1b0c174f5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ecacd70a-0d41-5ace-a88e-64b07dd6c585" "answer-cc660814-0552-58be-a5ff-bf43da8972f5" "answer-7d93b2a2-ea70-5d27-a06b-2eb1b0c174f5" "answer-48caa462-32f1-501c-83c0-0379aaf59677" "answer-6c04b536-8c47-5b60-84d0-ad4f649d58d1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ecacd70a-0d41-5ace-a88e-64b07dd6c585" :answer/id #uuid "ecacd70a-0d41-5ace-a88e-64b07dd6c585" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[2(2+\\frac{3j}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc660814-0552-58be-a5ff-bf43da8972f5" :answer/id #uuid "cc660814-0552-58be-a5ff-bf43da8972f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[2{(2+\\frac{2j}{n})}^{1/3}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d93b2a2-ea70-5d27-a06b-2eb1b0c174f5" :answer/id #uuid "7d93b2a2-ea70-5d27-a06b-2eb1b0c174f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[2{(2+\\frac{3j}{n})}^{1/3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48caa462-32f1-501c-83c0-0379aaf59677" :answer/id #uuid "48caa462-32f1-501c-83c0-0379aaf59677" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[2{(\\frac{3j}{n})}^{1/3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c04b536-8c47-5b60-84d0-ad4f649d58d1" :answer/id #uuid "6c04b536-8c47-5b60-84d0-ad4f649d58d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[{(3+\\frac{3j}{n})}^{1/3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186319081 :question/worked-solution "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=-1.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{3}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{n}=\\frac{b-(-1)}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nConsequently, ${x}_{k}=-1+\\frac{3k}{n}$ and $f({x}_{k})=({x}_{k}+8)^{1/3}.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(x+8)^{1/3}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[{((-1+\\frac{3k}{n})+8)}^{1/3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \n\n$$\nf(x)=(x+8)^{1/3}\\,\\text{and}\\,b=2.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186232563 :answer-field/correct "answer-f2efb08c-a787-5702-bd96-8a581319d3f2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f2efb08c-a787-5702-bd96-8a581319d3f2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2efb08c-a787-5702-bd96-8a581319d3f2" :answer/id #uuid "f2efb08c-a787-5702-bd96-8a581319d3f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-94a24590-9d5e-597a-b9fc-4e27a31e8bcf" :question/id #uuid "94a24590-9d5e-597a-b9fc-4e27a31e8bcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-346215" :question/problem "What is ${\\int }_{1}^{4}(x+8)^{1/3}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?\n\n*Hint: Write down the missing expression in terms of $i$ and $n.$*\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{4}(x+8)^{1/3}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[($\n{{field-1}}\n$)^{1/3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]$" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}(x+8)^{1/3}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=(x+8)^{1/3},$ the lower bound is $a=1$ and the upper bound is $b=4.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-1}{n}=\\frac{3}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(x+8)^{1/3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[f(1+i\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[f(1+\\frac{3i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[{((1+\\frac{3i}{n})+8)}^{1/3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[{(\\,9+\\frac{3i}{n}\\,)}^{1/3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-51c68f43-b8a4-56b8-87d9-4c3c430d2953"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-51c68f43-b8a4-56b8-87d9-4c3c430d2953" :answer-field/id #uuid "51c68f43-b8a4-56b8-87d9-4c3c430d2953" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a8e489ef-e019-5aa8-aaf8-81867e60a7e0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a8e489ef-e019-5aa8-aaf8-81867e60a7e0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8e489ef-e019-5aa8-aaf8-81867e60a7e0" :answer/id #uuid "a8e489ef-e019-5aa8-aaf8-81867e60a7e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9+\\frac{3i}{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4bc9664f-fb9e-55ce-8ee2-e0e93f2cfcb5" :question/id #uuid "4bc9664f-fb9e-55ce-8ee2-e0e93f2cfcb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-73181" :question/problem "What is ${\\int }_{-4}^{-1}\\sqrt{5}{x}^{-4}\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}\\sqrt{5}{x}^{-4}\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=\\sqrt{5}{x}^{-4},$ the lower bound is $a=-4$ and the upper bound is $b=-1.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{-1-(-4)}{n}=\\frac{3}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}\\sqrt{5}{x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[f(-4+i\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[f(-4+\\frac{3i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[\\sqrt{5}{(-4+\\frac{3i}{n})}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-64a07a31-890d-5a37-87c6-b4aa072b0cdd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-64a07a31-890d-5a37-87c6-b4aa072b0cdd" :answer-field/id #uuid "64a07a31-890d-5a37-87c6-b4aa072b0cdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8a534c45-0804-5cd0-ae1c-1bc24876ba0d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-638558e4-10ff-5afa-8bdf-9b786167c462" "answer-a6839a44-5f1b-5130-ad49-d3732b17ae53" "answer-b39b6574-f45a-534f-b0b8-98abbfe720be" "answer-8a534c45-0804-5cd0-ae1c-1bc24876ba0d" "answer-c308f5cd-baeb-5d55-a3e9-11c3b9fac238"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-638558e4-10ff-5afa-8bdf-9b786167c462" :answer/id #uuid "638558e4-10ff-5afa-8bdf-9b786167c462" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[5\\sqrt{-2+\\frac{5i}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6839a44-5f1b-5130-ad49-d3732b17ae53" :answer/id #uuid "a6839a44-5f1b-5130-ad49-d3732b17ae53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[5\\sqrt{-4+\\frac{3i}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b39b6574-f45a-534f-b0b8-98abbfe720be" :answer/id #uuid "b39b6574-f45a-534f-b0b8-98abbfe720be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[\\sqrt{5}{(-2+\\frac{3i}{n})}^{-2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a534c45-0804-5cd0-ae1c-1bc24876ba0d" :answer/id #uuid "8a534c45-0804-5cd0-ae1c-1bc24876ba0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[\\sqrt{5}{(-4+\\frac{3i}{n})}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c308f5cd-baeb-5d55-a3e9-11c3b9fac238" :answer/id #uuid "c308f5cd-baeb-5d55-a3e9-11c3b9fac238" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[{(-4+\\frac{2i}{n})}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3c8de7d3-85f5-5987-bc43-0d9881c2dbaf" :question/id #uuid "3c8de7d3-85f5-5987-bc43-0d9881c2dbaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-346205" :question/problem "What is ${\\int }_{2}^{5}8{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?\n\n*Hint: Write down the missing expression in terms of $i$ and $n.$*\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{5}8{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[8($\n{{field-1}}\n$)^{\\,4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]$" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{5}8{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=8{x}^{4},$ the lower bound is $a=2$ and the upper bound is $b=5.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{5-2}{n}=\\frac{3}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{5}8{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[f(2+i\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[f(2+\\frac{3i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[8{(\\,2+\\frac{3i}{n}\\,)}^{\\,4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b815cf32-0620-5ec8-861b-849fda16a0a3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b815cf32-0620-5ec8-861b-849fda16a0a3" :answer-field/id #uuid "b815cf32-0620-5ec8-861b-849fda16a0a3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d5ab0f54-2397-5b21-9e48-6a667621b28e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d5ab0f54-2397-5b21-9e48-6a667621b28e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5ab0f54-2397-5b21-9e48-6a667621b28e" :answer/id #uuid "d5ab0f54-2397-5b21-9e48-6a667621b28e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+\\frac{3i}{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186177819 :answer-field/choices 17592186177824] [:db/retract 17592186177819 :answer-field/choices 17592186177820] [:db/retract 17592186177819 :answer-field/choices 17592186177821] [:db/retract 17592186177819 :answer-field/choices 17592186177822] [:db/retract 17592186177819 :answer-field/choices 17592186177823] {:db/id 17592186179738 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b7927a26-b99a-5854-aa75-916116f0bbc7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180025 :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{C}z\\,\\text{d}x+x\\,\\text{d}y+y\\,\\text{d}z$ is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ for some piecewise smooth curve $C,$ then $F(x,y,z)=$" :question/worked-solution "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)\\,i+Q(x,y,z)\\,j+R(x,y,z)\\,k\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y+R\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nIn our case, $P=z,Q=x,R=y.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(z\\,i+x\\,j+y\\,k)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}z\\,\\text{d}x+x\\,\\text{d}y+y\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $F=z\\,i+x\\,j+y\\,k.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186177819 :answer-field/correct "answer-e4847fce-4e49-589a-b6ee-7837047bacf5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-754a17e4-04df-525d-9c6f-927705d19c10" "answer-0150bf9f-bc52-5d7c-baa1-278be0ec41d2" "answer-fe7ad197-686c-54ac-8451-0dbb07ea69a0" "answer-e4847fce-4e49-589a-b6ee-7837047bacf5" "answer-f52c058f-37bd-5f7c-a31f-2c35690a82a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-754a17e4-04df-525d-9c6f-927705d19c10" :answer/id #uuid "754a17e4-04df-525d-9c6f-927705d19c10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{2}\\,i+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0150bf9f-bc52-5d7c-baa1-278be0ec41d2" :answer/id #uuid "0150bf9f-bc52-5d7c-baa1-278be0ec41d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}∇(x+y+z)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe7ad197-686c-54ac-8451-0dbb07ea69a0" :answer/id #uuid "fe7ad197-686c-54ac-8451-0dbb07ea69a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4847fce-4e49-589a-b6ee-7837047bacf5" :answer/id #uuid "e4847fce-4e49-589a-b6ee-7837047bacf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z\\,i+x\\,j+y\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f52c058f-37bd-5f7c-a31f-2c35690a82a3" :answer/id #uuid "f52c058f-37bd-5f7c-a31f-2c35690a82a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∇(x+y+z)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b7927a26-b99a-5854-aa75-916116f0bbc7" :question/id #uuid "b7927a26-b99a-5854-aa75-916116f0bbc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-125411" :question/problem "Let $F(x,y,z)=yz\\,i+xz\\,j+xy\\,k$ and let $C$ be a path in ${R}^{3}.$ Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)\\,i+Q(x,y,z)\\,j+R(x,y,z)\\,k\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y+R(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}yz\\,\\text{d}x+xz\\,\\text{d}y+xy\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5f8c40bf-0ce0-5cf0-89dd-16aa652b7225"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5f8c40bf-0ce0-5cf0-89dd-16aa652b7225" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f8c40bf-0ce0-5cf0-89dd-16aa652b7225" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c30515bc-7147-5e35-a4a6-aa22b4d891de" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e80d1d5b-0eef-53d7-9609-23206eeed2a5" "answer-0abe0b0c-c7b6-54cc-89f5-b4e8765eb5d7" "answer-ae0c8d28-d367-5e4a-9fc3-ee267494558a" "answer-9d2c9102-5369-5ba0-ac8a-916120320f57" "answer-c30515bc-7147-5e35-a4a6-aa22b4d891de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e80d1d5b-0eef-53d7-9609-23206eeed2a5" :answer/id #uuid "e80d1d5b-0eef-53d7-9609-23206eeed2a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}(yz+xy+xy)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0abe0b0c-c7b6-54cc-89f5-b4e8765eb5d7" :answer/id #uuid "0abe0b0c-c7b6-54cc-89f5-b4e8765eb5d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}(yz+xz)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+xy\\,\\text{d}z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae0c8d28-d367-5e4a-9fc3-ee267494558a" :answer/id #uuid "ae0c8d28-d367-5e4a-9fc3-ee267494558a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}x\\,\\text{d}x+y\\,\\text{d}y+z\\,\\text{d}z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d2c9102-5369-5ba0-ac8a-916120320f57" :answer/id #uuid "9d2c9102-5369-5ba0-ac8a-916120320f57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}yz\\,\\text{d}x+(xz+xy)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c30515bc-7147-5e35-a4a6-aa22b4d891de" :answer/id #uuid "c30515bc-7147-5e35-a4a6-aa22b4d891de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}yz\\,\\text{d}x+xz\\,\\text{d}y+xy\\,\\text{d}z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180279 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed in counterclockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC={C}_{1}\\cup \\{-{C}_{2}\\}\\cup {C}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $-{C}_{2}$ is the same path as ${C}_{2}$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186345277 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed in counterclockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC={C}_{1}\\cup \\{-{C}_{2}\\}\\cup {C}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $-{C}_{2}$ is the same path as ${C}_{2}$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186415772 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed in counterclockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC=\\{-{C}_{1}\\}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $-{C}_{1}$ is the same path as ${C}_{1}$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180280 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed clockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC=\\{-{C}_{1}\\}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup \\{-{C}_{3}\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $-{C}_{1}$ and $-{C}_{3}$ are the same paths as ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{3}$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186345275 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed in clockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC=\\{-{C}_{1}\\}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $-{C}_{1}$ is the same path as ${C}_{1}$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
